# =====================================================================================
# foundation.queries.sparql — the EXPECT-TRUE ASK suite of the Foundation floor (W2 · SP0).
# =====================================================================================
# Auto-discovered by basicttl/foundation/checks/run-foundation-checks.sh: the runner splits
# this file on every "# EXPECT-TRUE <name>" marker and requires each ASK true over the merged
# SP0 + SP1 + SP2 + SP3 graph. Each ASK is non-vacuous (must return FALSE on the empty graph),
# carries an inline DATA CONTRACT naming the triples that make it true, and is proven to flip
# True -> False under a documented probe of record (mirroring its SHACL shape).
#
# T1 SCAFFOLD: no ASK is declared yet, so the runner reports "foundation ASKs: 0 run, 0 failed"
# and the floor is GREEN on the empty foundation graph. Each later task adds its EXPECT-TRUE
# ASK(s) here:
#
#   T2  q_engine_presents            every rung resolves to a (Sigma, E) presented algebra
#   T3  q_set_carrier                every foundation carrier is a fnd:Set under a grounding
#   T3  q_membership_typed           each element-of edge is 1->A typed
#   T3  q_universal_product          each product carries its two projections + factoriser
#   T3  q_presheaf_not_set           no presheaf is owl:sameAs its set of elements (PIN guard)
#   T4  q_magma_closure              closure holds on every enumerated-carrier fnd:Magma (op-result in the carrier)
#   T4  q_semigroup_assoc            associativity holds on the semigroup witness
#   T4  q_monoid_identity            the two-sided identity holds on the monoid witness
#   T4  q_commmonoid_comm            commutativity holds on the commutative-monoid witness
#   T4  q_group_inverse              the two-sided inverse undoes the op (SYN inverse law, cited)
#   T4  q_abelian_comm               commutativity holds on the abelian-group witness
#   T4  q_quasigroup_division        Latin-square division holds on the quasigroup family (quasigroup + loop)
#   T4  q_quasigroup_total           Latin-square division is TOTAL (every a,b has a left AND right solution) (A2)
#   T4  q_loop_identity              the two-sided identity holds on every fnd:Loop witness (L1 close)
#   T4  q_monoid_is_endo             Monoid ~= one-object category ~= F(X,X) (Pillar-4 seam)
#   T5  q_ring_distrib               distributivity holds on the ring witness
#   T5  q_ring_add_assoc             additive associativity holds on every fnd:Semiring ((a+b)+c=a+(b+c)) (A1)
#   T5  q_ring_add_comm              additive commutativity holds on every fnd:Semiring (a+b=b+a) (A1)
#   T5  q_ring_mult_assoc            multiplicative associativity holds on every fnd:Semiring ((a*b)*c=a*(b*c)) (A1)
#   T5  q_field_mult_inverse         every nonzero field element is multiplicatively invertible
#   T5  q_module_scalar              the scalar action is well TYPED on every fnd:Module (R x M -> M)
#   T5  q_module_scalar_law          the FULL module scalar-action law (unitality + scalar-assoc + bi-distrib) (W-SP0-B)
#   T5  q_vectorspace_axioms         the 8 vector-space axioms hold over a fnd:Field
#   T6  q_sheaf_glues                agreeing local sections glue to a unique global section
#   T6  q_topology_axioms            tau closed under finite intersection + arbitrary union
#   T6  q_metric_triangle            d satisfies identity / symmetry / triangle inequality
#   T7  q_frame_is_functionality     prim:Frame is recognized as Curry's functionality F
#   T7  q_functor_variance           the variance bifunctor is contravariant dom / covariant cod
#   T7  q_no_untyped_self_apply      a chi-chi is provisional unless GENUINELY resolved (Fix-C: passedGuard -> a fnd:ContractGate/fnd:QuarantineResolution marking it provisional)
#   T8  q_combinator_reduces         each combinator's defining reduction holds
#   T8  q_fn_ladder                  the F_n recurrence holds across the ladder
#   T9  q_implication_kcw            the K / C / W implication laws hold
#   T9  q_curry_howard               exponential B^A and implication A superset B coincide
#   T10 q_reanchor_additive          every prior-floor grounding is an edge; no prior triple removed
#   T10 q_sealedgroup_is_group       the SP2 SealedGroup satisfies the full fnd:Group teeth
# =====================================================================================


# EXPECT-TRUE q_engine_presents : every presented algebra is MINTED by the engine (Sigma + E + F_E-carrier).
#   The minting engine LIFTED from Helios (design s1; ledger/W2/algebra_foundation/02_algebra_tower.md s2):
#   Helios authors the presented free algebra on a many-sorted signature-with-equations F_E(X)=T_Sigma(X)/=_E
#   (helios/srcy/papers/26_adjunctions_free_graphs_governed_algebras/chapters/03_free_functor_on_graphs/
#   sections/03_signature_equations_governed.tex:31-42) plus the free-|forgetful adjunction L-|R with
#   unit eta / counit epsilon (26/sections/01_thesis.tex:93-128) and the GovAlg wrapper (A,op,E,V,l,P)
#   (26/chapters/04/sections/01_governed_algebra_definition.tex:6-13). A rung is not hand-axiomatised: it
#   is a fnd:PresentedAlgebra whose carrier is F_E(X)-produced by the LIFTED engine and whose asserted
#   laws all live in its equation set. This is what makes "the tower is minted, not invented" a graph fact.
#   DATA CONTRACT (engine.ttl): at least one ?w a fnd:PresentedAlgebra exists (non-vacuity anchor, FALSE on
#     the empty foundation graph); EVERY ?pa a fnd:PresentedAlgebra carries (1) a fnd:hasSignature (its
#     Sigma), (2) a fnd:hasEquationSet (its E), (3) a fnd:hasCarrier ?c that is fnd:mintedVia a
#     fnd:FreeForgetful (the carrier is F_E-produced by the engine, not asserted free by fiat), (4)
#     every fnd:satisfiesLaw ?law it claims is a fnd:hasEquation member of its own equation set (no law
#     outside E - the E-must-not-EXCEED direction), and (5, the E-COVERAGE strengthening) every law it
#     fnd:rungRequiresLaw (a law a class-general tooth enforces on it) is one it fnd:satisfiesLaw (its
#     presentation COVERS every enforced law - the E-must-COVER direction; clauses 4+5 together pin
#     fnd:satisfiesLaw == the enforced law set, so E genuinely PRESENTS the rung, matching algebra_spine.ttl).
#     The witness fnd:witnessPresentedAlgebra (Sigma=fnd:witnessSignature, E=fnd:witnessEquationSet
#     with member fnd:witnessLaw, carrier fnd:witnessCarrier mintedVia fnd:engineAdjunction, satisfiesLaw
#     fnd:witnessLaw) satisfies clauses 1-4 and carries no fnd:rungRequiresLaw (clause 5 vacuous); each
#     two-operation rung fnd:Semiring..fnd:VectorSpace has fnd:rungRequiresLaw a SUBSET of its fnd:satisfiesLaw.
#   PROBE OF RECORD (must flip True->False, mirrored by fnd:PresentedAlgebraShape): (a) remove
#     fnd:witnessCarrier fnd:mintedVia fnd:engineAdjunction (a carrier NOT produced by F_E) -> clause 3
#     fails; (b) add fnd:witnessPresentedAlgebra fnd:satisfiesLaw fnd:foreignLaw where fnd:foreignLaw is
#     NOT fnd:hasEquation of fnd:witnessEquationSet (a rung claiming a law not in its E) -> clause 4 fails;
#     (c) delete fnd:Semiring fnd:satisfiesLaw fnd:lawAddAssoc while fnd:Semiring still fnd:rungRequiresLaw
#     fnd:lawAddAssoc and fnd:RingAddAssocShape still enforces additive associativity on every fnd:Semiring
#     (a rung whose presentation OMITS an enforced law) -> clause 5 fails.
PREFIX fnd: <urn:silmaril:fnd:#>
ASK {
  ?w a fnd:PresentedAlgebra .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?pa a fnd:PresentedAlgebra .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?pa fnd:hasSignature ?s }
  }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?pa a fnd:PresentedAlgebra .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?pa fnd:hasEquationSet ?e }
  }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?pa a fnd:PresentedAlgebra .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?pa fnd:hasCarrier ?c . ?c fnd:mintedVia ?ff . ?ff a fnd:FreeForgetful }
  }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?pa a fnd:PresentedAlgebra ; fnd:satisfiesLaw ?law ; fnd:hasEquationSet ?e .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?e fnd:hasEquation ?law }
  }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?pa fnd:rungRequiresLaw ?law .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?pa fnd:satisfiesLaw ?law }
  }
}

# EXPECT-TRUE q_set_carrier : every foundation carrier is a fnd:Set under a forgetful grounding.
#   The structural Set floor (design s2, Pillar 1; ledger/W2/algebra_foundation/03_set_theory.md s1-s4).
#   Helios takes Set as the AMBIENT codomain of every presheaf P:C^op->Set (LIFTED,
#   helios/srcy/papers/18_presheaf_semantics/sections/01_thesis.tex:24-31,59-68) but never descends
#   into it - that descent is the foundation's job, and it is the honest TWO-STEP descent. The engine's
#   lifted right adjoint R:GovAlg->Graph (engine.ttl fnd:rightAdjoint, DS,
#   helios/srcy/papers/26_adjunctions_free_graphs_governed_algebras/sections/01_thesis.tex:93-101) forgets
#   a governed algebra to its underlying GRAPH (Hom_GovAlg(LG,A) ~= Hom_Graph(G,RA)); the Graph->Set
#   underlying-vertex-set forgetful functor (fnd:graphUnderlyingSet, SYN standard math, NOT a paper-26
#   lift) THEN sends that graph to the underlying set of the free-algebra carrier F_E(X) - never a single
#   DS R:GovAlg->Set. This tooth makes that a graph fact: every foundation carrier
#   (a fnd:FreeAlgebra, the engine's produced carrier object) must carry a fnd:groundsInSet edge into a
#   fnd:Set - a carrier IS a Set under a forgetful grounding, NOT a subtype (design s7 edge mechanism,
#   mirroring SP3's crs:ForgetfulTagFrame surjection and SP1's prim:DualGroundingShape realizes-edge
#   discipline). The grounding is checked by EDGE EXISTENCE on the carrier (never a range-inferred
#   rdf:type), so inference=rdfs cannot forge it and defang the tooth.
#   DATA CONTRACT (set_theory.ttl + engine.ttl): at least one ?c a fnd:FreeAlgebra exists (non-vacuity
#     anchor, FALSE on the empty graph - fnd:witnessCarrier from engine.ttl); and EVERY ?fa a
#     fnd:FreeAlgebra carries a fnd:groundsInSet ?s edge (fnd:witnessCarrier fnd:groundsInSet
#     fnd:witnessUnderlyingSet, with fnd:witnessUnderlyingSet a fnd:Set). fnd:groundsInSet declares the
#     permissive rdfs:range owl:Thing, not the precise fnd:Set (each target is typed rdf:type fnd:Set
#     EXPLICITLY, so the ReanchorLandingParityShape positive landing test is not defanged by range-forging);
#     the tooth reads only the carrier's outgoing edge.
#   PROBE OF RECORD (must flip True->False, mirrored by fnd:SetCarrierShape): inject a carrier with no
#     grounding - fnd:probeUngroundedCarrier a fnd:FreeAlgebra (no fnd:groundsInSet edge) - a free-algebra
#     carrier that is not grounded into any set; the inner FILTER NOT EXISTS finds it and the ASK is FALSE.
PREFIX fnd: <urn:silmaril:fnd:#>
ASK {
  ?c a fnd:FreeAlgebra .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?fa a fnd:FreeAlgebra .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?fa fnd:groundsInSet ?s }
  }
}


# EXPECT-TRUE q_membership_typed : every membership edge is a global element 1->A (typed, not bare).
#   Structural membership (design s2, Pillar 1; 03_set_theory.md s2.1). Helios USES membership
#   operationally (x in P(A), the category of elements Ob(int P)={(c,x)|c in Ob(C), x in P(c)},
#   18/chapters/04/sections/01_category_of_elements.tex:10-20) but authors NO first-class typed
#   membership primitive. This tooth fills that gap the structural (ETCS) way: an element x of a set A
#   is a GLOBAL ELEMENT, a function 1->A from the terminal object fnd:Unit into A. A fnd:elementOf edge
#   is well typed exactly when its subject is such an arrow: fnd:hasDomain fnd:Unit and fnd:hasCodomain
#   the very set it is an element of. This keeps membership from collapsing into a bare untyped link.
#   DATA CONTRACT (set_theory.ttl): at least one ?x fnd:elementOf ?A exists (non-vacuity anchor, FALSE
#     on the empty graph - fnd:witnessElement fnd:elementOf fnd:witnessSetA); and EVERY ?e fnd:elementOf
#     ?A satisfies ?e fnd:hasDomain fnd:Unit and ?e fnd:hasCodomain ?A (fnd:witnessElement a
#     fnd:GlobalElement ; fnd:hasDomain fnd:Unit ; fnd:hasCodomain fnd:witnessSetA).
#   PROBE OF RECORD (must flip True->False, mirrored by fnd:MembershipTypedShape): inject an untyped
#     membership - fnd:probeUntypedElement fnd:elementOf fnd:witnessSetA (with NO fnd:hasDomain fnd:Unit)
#     - an element that is not the arrow 1->A; the inner FILTER NOT EXISTS finds it and the ASK is FALSE.
PREFIX fnd: <urn:silmaril:fnd:#>
ASK {
  ?x fnd:elementOf ?A .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?e fnd:elementOf ?B .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?e fnd:hasDomain fnd:Unit . ?e fnd:hasCodomain ?B }
  }
}


# EXPECT-TRUE q_universal_product : every product carries its two projections + a universal factoriser.
#   The universal-construction product (design s2, Pillar 1; 03_set_theory.md s2.4), held DISTINCT from
#   the DATA product prim:Tuple (SP6 polysemy, D-SET-5). Products are well covered in Helios as USAGE
#   (data prim:Tuple + terminal prim:Unit, the ordered pairs (c,x) of the category of elements, the SP3
#   five-factor product K with its pi_j joint-faithfulness seal, crs/README.md:37-38); this tooth reifies
#   the UNIVERSAL PROPERTY as a first-class object the same way aob:group_law reifies the colimit: a
#   fnd:Product must carry its two projections (fnd:hasProjection pi_1, pi_2, distinct) AND the unique
#   universal factoriser (fnd:hasFactoriser, the mediating <f,g> from any cone). A product missing a
#   projection or the factoriser is not a genuine categorical product and is rejected.
#   DATA CONTRACT (set_theory.ttl): at least one ?p a fnd:Product exists (non-vacuity anchor, FALSE on
#     the empty graph - fnd:witnessProduct); and EVERY ?pr a fnd:Product carries two DISTINCT
#     fnd:hasProjection and at least one fnd:hasFactoriser (fnd:witnessProduct fnd:hasProjection
#     fnd:witnessProj1, fnd:witnessProj2 ; fnd:hasFactoriser fnd:witnessFactoriser).
#   PROBE OF RECORD (must flip True->False, mirrored by fnd:UniversalProductShape): inject a deficient
#     product - fnd:probeBadProduct a fnd:Product (no projections, no factoriser) - a product without its
#     universal property; the inner FILTER NOT EXISTS finds it and the ASK is FALSE.
PREFIX fnd: <urn:silmaril:fnd:#>
ASK {
  ?p a fnd:Product .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?pr a fnd:Product .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS {
      ?pr fnd:hasProjection ?p1 , ?p2 . FILTER(?p1 != ?p2)
      ?pr fnd:hasFactoriser ?f .
    }
  }
}


# EXPECT-TRUE q_presheaf_not_set : no presheaf is owl:sameAs its own set of elements (the PIN guard).
#   The load-bearing set-floor LAW, not a caveat (design s2 PIN guard; 03_set_theory.md D-SET-6). Helios
#   names the "forbidden collapse" explicitly: identifying the presheaf P with the set of elements P(c)
#   "drops the contravariant action and collapses functoriality into static labelling, which is the
#   cheese-trap face this volume is most exposed to" (18/sections/01_thesis.tex:65-68). The set floor is
#   the CARRIER beneath the category layer; it must NOT flatten it (X = Hom(-,X) is shorthand, not
#   identity - 14/sections/01_thesis.tex:90-102). This tooth makes the guard a graph fact: a presheaf
#   (fnd:Presheaf, P:C^op->Set) and its element-set P(c) (fnd:presheafElementSet, a fnd:Set) are DISTINCT
#   objects; asserting fnd:witnessPresheaf owl:sameAs its element-set is precisely the collapse and is RED.
#   DATA CONTRACT (set_theory.ttl): at least one ?p a fnd:Presheaf with a fnd:presheafElementSet exists
#     (non-vacuity anchor, FALSE on the empty graph - fnd:witnessPresheaf fnd:presheafElementSet
#     fnd:witnessPresheafElemSet); and NO presheaf is owl:sameAs its own element-set (on the happy path
#     the two nodes are deliberately kept distinct - no owl:sameAs between them).
#   PROBE OF RECORD (must flip True->False, mirrored by fnd:PresheafNotSetShape): inject the collapse -
#     fnd:witnessPresheaf owl:sameAs fnd:witnessPresheafElemSet - the presheaf identified with its set of
#     elements; the inner EXISTS finds it and the ASK is FALSE.
PREFIX fnd: <urn:silmaril:fnd:#>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
ASK {
  ?p a fnd:Presheaf ; fnd:presheafElementSet ?s0 .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?pp a fnd:Presheaf ; fnd:presheafElementSet ?s .
    ?pp owl:sameAs ?s .
  }
}


# EXPECT-TRUE q_magma_closure : closure/totality holds on every enumerated-carrier fnd:Magma (every op-result is a carrier element).
#   The one-operation spine, base MAGMA rung (design s3; ledger/W2/algebra_foundation/02_algebra_tower.md
#   s1 MAGMA). fnd:Magma is a CONCRETE law-bearing rung (fnd:addsLaw fnd:lawClosure), but its
#   closure/totality law - the binary operation . : S,S -> S is a TOTAL function landing in the carrier S -
#   previously had NO biting tooth and NO witness model, while every sibling rung (Semigroup..AbelianGroup,
#   Quasigroup/Loop) carried both (M1 parity defect). SYN, cited standard universal algebra (fnd:Magma is
#   SYN; the free term-algebra substrate T_Sigma(X) is LIFTED, 26/03/03:13-15). This tooth makes closure a
#   CHECKABLE graph fact by REUSING the SealedGroup closure idiom (fnd:SealedGroupIsGroupShape /
#   q_sealedgroup_is_group: a reified product over the op whose fnd:opResult is NOT a fnd:hasElement of the
#   structure -> violation), generalised CLASS-GENERAL over the fnd:Magma family: for EVERY fnd:Magma that
#   ENUMERATES its carrier (fnd:hasElement), every reified fnd:opResult over it MUST be one of its
#   fnd:hasElement. The enumerated-carrier guard is essential - the spine witnesses that do NOT enumerate a
#   carrier (fnd:semigroupModel..fnd:groupModel, fnd:quasigroupModel..fnd:loopModel) have no fnd:hasElement,
#   so they are not in scope and are not misread as all-escaping; the enumerated magmas are fnd:magmaModel
#   (the closed order-2 non-associative witness) and, via rdfs:subClassOf* fnd:Magma, the T10 aob:witnessGroup
#   (the closed Z/4 SealedGroup), both closed.
#   CLASS-GENERAL (no witness IRI hardcoded): QUANTIFIES OVER EVERY fnd:Magma instance via the property path
#   rdf:type/rdfs:subClassOf* fnd:Magma (the ASK suite runs over the RAW, non-inferred merged graph, so the
#   explicit subClassOf* chain reaches aob:witnessGroup a aob:SealedGroup rdfs:subClassOf fnd:Group ... fnd:Magma
#   as well as the direct fnd:magmaModel a fnd:Magma). The SHACL fnd:MagmaClosureShape does the same under
#   inference=rdfs (sh:targetClass fnd:Magma).
#   DATA CONTRACT (algebra_spine.ttl + reanchor.ttl): at least one fnd:Magma with an enumerated carrier + an
#     op row exists (non-vacuity anchor, FALSE on the empty graph - fnd:magmaModel fnd:hasElement fnd:elemA,
#     fnd:elemB with the four rows A.A=B, A.B=B, B.A=A, B.B=B, all landing in {A,B}); and NO fnd:Magma-typed
#     model that enumerates a carrier has a reified fnd:opResult that is not one of its fnd:hasElement (both
#     fnd:magmaModel and the Z/4 aob:witnessGroup are closed).
#   PROBE OF RECORD (must flip True->False, mirrored by fnd:MagmaClosureShape): inject a fnd:Magma with an
#     op-result outside its enumerated carrier - fnd:probeMagmaOpenResult a fnd:Magma ; fnd:hasElement
#     fnd:elemA , fnd:elemB with an op row whose fnd:opResult is fnd:elemC (NOT a fnd:hasElement of the magma)
#     - the inner EXISTS finds the escaping product and the ASK is FALSE; fnd:magmaModel stays GREEN.
PREFIX rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
PREFIX fnd: <urn:silmaril:fnd:#>
ASK {
  ?mAnchor rdf:type/rdfs:subClassOf* fnd:Magma ; fnd:hasElement ?anchorEl .
  ?anchorRow fnd:opStructure ?mAnchor .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?m rdf:type/rdfs:subClassOf* fnd:Magma ; fnd:hasElement ?el .
    ?row fnd:opStructure ?m ; fnd:opResult ?r .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?m fnd:hasElement ?r }
  }
}


# EXPECT-TRUE q_semigroup_assoc : associativity holds on the semigroup rung witness ((a.b).c == a.(b.c)).
#   The one-operation spine, Semigroup rung (design s3; ledger/W2/algebra_foundation/02_algebra_tower.md
#   s1 SEMIGROUP). Helios NAMES semigroup only once, as a boundary counterexample ("associativity
#   without a unit gives only a semigroup, not a monoid", helios/srcy/papers/21_ologs_and_typed_english/
#   chapters/05_yoneda_for_typed_english/sections/04_monoid_monad_yoneda_binders.tex:138), but the
#   associativity LAW itself is PROOF-DERIVED (PD): proved for path concatenation (31/chapters/01/sections/
#   02_free_path_category_construction.tex:51-94) and for the colon product of the ecosystem free monoid
#   (07/chapters/05/sections/03_ecosystem_free_monoid.tex:51-55). The Semigroup rung is a fnd:Magma + this
#   one added law (fnd:lawAssociativity, fnd:addsLaw), minted as a fnd:PresentedAlgebra through the LIFTED
#   engine. This tooth makes associativity a CHECKABLE graph fact over the reified binary-operation table of
#   the semigroup witness (fnd:semigroupModel, a left-zero semigroup x.y=x on {A,B,C}), mirroring SP2's
#   q_group_associativity (aob:Composition) one floor down: for any triple (x,y,z) the two bracketings
#   (x.y).z and x.(y.z) must evaluate to the SAME fnd:opResult.
#   CLASS-GENERAL (no witness IRI hardcoded): this ASK QUANTIFIES OVER EVERY fnd:Semigroup instance via the
#   property path rdf:type/rdfs:subClassOf* fnd:Semigroup (the ASK suite runs over the RAW, non-inferred
#   merged graph, so the explicit subClassOf* chain - not rdfs materialisation - is what reaches the
#   associative rungs above the base witness: fnd:Monoid/fnd:CommutativeMonoid/fnd:Group/fnd:AbelianGroup and
#   the SP2 aob:SealedGroup, each subClassOf fnd:Semigroup; the non-associative fnd:Quasigroup/fnd:Loop off
#   fnd:Magma is excluded). The SHACL fnd:SemigroupAssocShape does the same under inference=rdfs.
#   DATA CONTRACT (algebra_spine.ttl): at least one op row exists on some ?m a fnd:Semigroup (non-vacuity
#     anchor, FALSE on the empty graph - the left-zero rows A.B=A, A.C=A, B.C=B); and NO triple (x,y,z) over
#     ANY fnd:Semigroup-typed model has (x.y).z != x.(y.z) (the base witness, the Z/3 group, the abelian and
#     commutative-monoid fragments, the Z/4 sealed group, the Z/3 module additive group are all associative).
#   PROBE OF RECORD (must flip True->False, mirrored by fnd:SemigroupAssocShape): change fnd:appSgAC
#     fnd:opResult from fnd:elemA to fnd:elemB (so (A.B).C = A.C = B while A.(B.C) = A.B = A) - the inner
#     EXISTS finds the non-associative triple, and the ASK is FALSE; a FRESH non-associative fnd:Semigroup
#     instance flips it the same way (the tooth is class-general, not witness-pinned).
PREFIX rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
PREFIX fnd: <urn:silmaril:fnd:#>
ASK {
  ?mAnchor rdf:type/rdfs:subClassOf* fnd:Semigroup .
  ?anchor fnd:opStructure ?mAnchor .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?m rdf:type/rdfs:subClassOf* fnd:Semigroup .
    ?ab2  fnd:opStructure ?m ; fnd:opLeft ?x ; fnd:opRight ?y ; fnd:opResult ?xyr .
    ?lhs2 fnd:opStructure ?m ; fnd:opLeft ?xyr ; fnd:opRight ?z ; fnd:opResult ?lr .
    ?bc2  fnd:opStructure ?m ; fnd:opLeft ?y ; fnd:opRight ?z ; fnd:opResult ?yzr .
    ?rhs2 fnd:opStructure ?m ; fnd:opLeft ?x ; fnd:opRight ?yzr ; fnd:opResult ?rr .
    FILTER(?lr != ?rr)
  }
}


# EXPECT-TRUE q_monoid_identity : the two-sided identity holds on the monoid rung witness (e.x=x, x.e=x).
#   The one-operation spine, Monoid rung (design s3; 02_algebra_tower.md s1 MONOID) - the ONE genuinely
#   LIFTED rung (DS): Helios authors the monoid richly and provably (free monoid (E,:,eps) with proved
#   unit + associativity, 07/chapters/05/sections/03_ecosystem_free_monoid.tex:38-55; endopath monoid
#   M_X=Hom(X,X), 31/sections/01_thesis.tex:29-32; "monoid = one-object category", 21/05/04:2,16-17). The
#   two-sided identity/unit LAW is proof-derived (PD, the free-monoid unit proof). The Monoid rung is a
#   fnd:Semigroup + this one added law (fnd:lawIdentity, fnd:addsLaw), minted as a fnd:PresentedAlgebra.
#   This tooth makes the two-sided identity a CHECKABLE graph fact: a structure that declares an identity
#   element (fnd:hasIdentityElement e) must have e.x = x and x.e = x for every reified op row.
#   DATA CONTRACT (algebra_spine.ttl): at least one structure carries fnd:hasIdentityElement (non-vacuity
#     anchor, FALSE on the empty graph - fnd:monoidModel fnd:hasIdentityElement fnd:elemE, with rows
#     E.A=A, A.E=A, E.E=E over fnd:opStructure fnd:monoidModel); and for EVERY structure ?m with
#     fnd:hasIdentityElement ?e, NO op row of ?m with ?e on the left has a result != its right operand, and
#     NO op row with ?e on the right has a result != its left operand.
#   PROBE OF RECORD (must flip True->False, mirrored by fnd:MonoidIdentityShape): change fnd:appMonEA
#     fnd:opResult from fnd:elemA to fnd:elemE (so E.A = E != A) - the declared identity fails the left-unit
#     law, the inner UNION finds the offending row, and the ASK is FALSE.
PREFIX rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
PREFIX fnd: <urn:silmaril:fnd:#>
ASK {
  ?m fnd:hasIdentityElement ?e0 .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?mm fnd:hasIdentityElement ?e .
    {
      ?rL fnd:opStructure ?mm ; fnd:opLeft ?e ; fnd:opRight ?x ; fnd:opResult ?rLr .
      FILTER(?rLr != ?x)
    } UNION {
      ?rR fnd:opStructure ?mm ; fnd:opLeft ?x ; fnd:opRight ?e ; fnd:opResult ?rRr .
      FILTER(?rRr != ?x)
    }
  }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?mono rdf:type/rdfs:subClassOf* fnd:Monoid .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?mono fnd:hasIdentityElement ?eX }
  }
}


# EXPECT-TRUE q_commmonoid_comm : commutativity holds on the commutative-monoid rung witness (x.y=y.x).
#   The one-operation spine, CommutativeMonoid rung (design s3; 02_algebra_tower.md s1 COMMUTATIVE MONOID) -
#   SYN (the ATOM synthesized; instances lifted: (N0,+,0) as a grading target 31/02/03:10, M_J=N0^J
#   26/10/01:8; commutativity as a DECLARED congruence in the trace monoid E/=_I, 07/05/03:222-232;
#   noncommutativity is the explicit corpus default, ba != ab, 31/02/03:12-15). The CommutativeMonoid rung
#   is a fnd:Monoid + this one added law (fnd:lawCommutativity, fnd:addsLaw), minted as a
#   fnd:PresentedAlgebra. This tooth makes commutativity a CHECKABLE graph fact over the reified op table of
#   the commutative-monoid witness (fnd:commMonoidModel): NO pair (x,y) has x.y != y.x.
#   CLASS-GENERAL (no witness IRI hardcoded): QUANTIFIES OVER EVERY fnd:CommutativeMonoid instance via
#   rdf:type/rdfs:subClassOf* fnd:CommutativeMonoid (raw-graph property path, mirroring the SHACL
#   fnd:CommMonoidCommShape under inference=rdfs).
#   DATA CONTRACT (algebra_spine.ttl): at least one op row exists on some ?m a fnd:CommutativeMonoid
#     (non-vacuity anchor, FALSE on the empty graph - the symmetric rows A.B=E and B.A=E); and NO pair (x,y)
#     over ANY fnd:CommutativeMonoid-typed model has x.y != y.x.
#   PROBE OF RECORD (must flip True->False, mirrored by fnd:CommMonoidCommShape): change fnd:appCmBA
#     fnd:opResult from fnd:elemE to fnd:elemA (so B.A = A while A.B = E) - the inner EXISTS finds it, and the
#     ASK is FALSE; a FRESH non-commutative fnd:CommutativeMonoid instance flips it the same way.
PREFIX rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
PREFIX fnd: <urn:silmaril:fnd:#>
ASK {
  ?mAnchor rdf:type/rdfs:subClassOf* fnd:CommutativeMonoid .
  ?anchor fnd:opStructure ?mAnchor ; fnd:opLeft ?la ; fnd:opRight ?ra ; fnd:opResult ?resa .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?m rdf:type/rdfs:subClassOf* fnd:CommutativeMonoid .
    ?xy fnd:opStructure ?m ; fnd:opLeft ?x ; fnd:opRight ?y ; fnd:opResult ?xyr .
    ?yx fnd:opStructure ?m ; fnd:opLeft ?y ; fnd:opRight ?x ; fnd:opResult ?yxr .
    FILTER(?xyr != ?yxr)
  }
}


# EXPECT-TRUE q_group_inverse : the two-sided inverse undoes the operation on the group rung witness.
#   The one-operation spine, Group rung (design s3; 02_algebra_tower.md s1 GROUP) - SYN, and the INVERSE
#   LAW is the ONE tower axiom with ZERO Helios basis (02_algebra_tower.md s1: "the inverse/invertibility
#   axiom is never defined for any ontology structure"; every corpus 'invertible' hit is cocone-leg /
#   comparison-map invertibility, not a group inverse). It is authored as CITED STANDARD-MATHEMATICAL FACT
#   (the Directive-19/20 precedent: math is fact and liftable, cite the source, never pretend a Helios
#   lift). The Group rung is a fnd:Monoid + this one added law (fnd:lawInverse, fnd:addsLaw), minted as a
#   fnd:PresentedAlgebra. This tooth reuses the SP2 sealed-group inverse-teeth pattern (a retract that does
#   not undo -> RED, aob:retracts): a claimed inverse pairing (fnd:InversePairing: element x, inverse y in
#   a model with identity e) is GENUINE only if x.y = e AND y.x = e (two-sided undo).
#   DATA CONTRACT (algebra_spine.ttl): at least one fnd:InversePairing exists (non-vacuity anchor, FALSE on
#     the empty graph - fnd:invPairAB pairs A with B in fnd:groupModel, whose fnd:hasIdentityElement is
#     fnd:elemE, with rows A.B=E and B.A=E); for EVERY fnd:InversePairing (model ?mdl, element ?x,
#     inverse ?y) with ?mdl fnd:hasIdentityElement ?e, BOTH ?x.?y = ?e AND ?y.?x = ?e hold (GENUINENESS);
#     AND (W1b, COMPLETENESS) EVERY fnd:hasGroupElement of a fnd:Group carries an fnd:InversePairing with it
#     as fnd:pairingElement (fnd:groupModel enumerates E/A/B, each with a pairing).
#   PROBE OF RECORD (must flip True->False, mirrored by fnd:GroupInverseShape): (genuineness) change
#     fnd:appGrAB fnd:opResult from fnd:elemE to fnd:elemA (so A.B = A != e) - the claimed inverse B no
#     longer undoes A, the inner two-sided-undo FILTER NOT EXISTS fails for fnd:invPairAB, and the ASK is
#     FALSE; (completeness, W1b) a fnd:Group over {E,A} with A non-invertible and an fnd:InversePairing only
#     for E - the completeness FILTER NOT EXISTS finds a group element with no pairing, and the ASK is FALSE.
PREFIX rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
PREFIX fnd: <urn:silmaril:fnd:#>
ASK {
  ?p a fnd:InversePairing .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?pp a fnd:InversePairing ; fnd:pairingModel ?mdl ; fnd:pairingElement ?x ; fnd:pairingInverse ?y .
    ?mdl fnd:hasIdentityElement ?e .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS {
      ?xy fnd:opStructure ?mdl ; fnd:opLeft ?x ; fnd:opRight ?y ; fnd:opResult ?e .
      ?yx fnd:opStructure ?mdl ; fnd:opLeft ?y ; fnd:opRight ?x ; fnd:opResult ?e .
    }
  }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?grp a fnd:Group ; fnd:hasGroupElement ?ge .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?pc a fnd:InversePairing ; fnd:pairingModel ?grp ; fnd:pairingElement ?ge }
  }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?grpC rdf:type/rdfs:subClassOf* fnd:Group .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { { ?grpC fnd:hasGroupElement ?gx } UNION { ?grpC fnd:hasElement ?hx } }
  }
}


# EXPECT-TRUE q_abelian_comm : commutativity holds on the abelian-group rung witness (x.y=y.x).
