# EXPECT-TRUE q_quasigroup_division : Latin-square division holds on the quasigroup rung witness.
#   The division sub-family, Quasigroup rung (design s3; 02_algebra_tower.md s1 QUASIGROUP/LOOP - fully
#   ABSENT in Helios, grep zero) - SYN, cited standard math. A quasigroup is a fnd:Magma whose Cayley
#   table is a LATIN SQUARE: for every a,b the equations a.x=b and y.a=b have UNIQUE solutions (right and
#   left division). The Quasigroup rung is a fnd:Magma + this one added law (fnd:lawLatinDivision,
#   fnd:addsLaw), minted as a fnd:PresentedAlgebra. This tooth makes the Latin-square property a CHECKABLE
#   graph fact over the reified op tables of the fnd:Quasigroup FAMILY (fnd:quasigroupModel, the cyclic Z/3
#   table on {A,B,C}, AND - generalised at L1 - fnd:loopModel, the order-5 loop, a fnd:Quasigroup by
#   subclass): within each quasigroup model no row repeats a result (right-division uniqueness) and no column
#   repeats a result (left-division uniqueness) - the defining property of a quasigroup Cayley table. This is
#   the tooth that WITNESSES fnd:loopModel's inherited Latin-square/division law (its ADDED-law tooth is the
#   identity, q_loop_identity).
#   DATA CONTRACT (algebra_spine.ttl): at least one op row over some ?qg a fnd:Quasigroup exists
#     (non-vacuity anchor, FALSE on the empty graph - the 9-row cyclic Latin square A.A=A,A.B=B,A.C=C,
#     B.A=B,B.B=C,B.C=A,C.A=C,C.B=A,C.C=B AND the 25-row order-5 loop Latin square); for EVERY ?qg a
#     fnd:Quasigroup, NO fixed left operand a yields the same result for two DISTINCT right operands
#     (right-division uniqueness), and NO fixed right operand a yields the same result for two DISTINCT left
#     operands (left-division uniqueness). The ?qg a fnd:Quasigroup guard is essential - without it the
#     non-Latin fnd:semigroupModel / fnd:monoidModel rows would be misread as collisions.
#   PROBE OF RECORD (must flip True->False, mirrored by fnd:QuasigroupDivisionShape): change fnd:appQgAC
#     fnd:opResult from fnd:elemC to fnd:elemB (so the quasigroup A-row has A.B=B AND A.C=B, two right-divisors
#     of B under A) - right-division is no longer unique, the inner EXISTS finds the collision, ASK is FALSE.
PREFIX fnd: <urn:silmaril:fnd:#>
ASK {
  ?anchor fnd:opStructure ?qg0 . ?qg0 a fnd:Quasigroup .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?qg a fnd:Quasigroup .
    ?r1 fnd:opStructure ?qg ; fnd:opLeft ?a ; fnd:opRight ?x1 ; fnd:opResult ?r .
    ?r2 fnd:opStructure ?qg ; fnd:opLeft ?a ; fnd:opRight ?x2 ; fnd:opResult ?r .
    FILTER(?x1 != ?x2)
  }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?qg a fnd:Quasigroup .
    ?l1 fnd:opStructure ?qg ; fnd:opLeft ?y1 ; fnd:opRight ?b ; fnd:opResult ?s .
    ?l2 fnd:opStructure ?qg ; fnd:opLeft ?y2 ; fnd:opRight ?b ; fnd:opResult ?s .
    FILTER(?y1 != ?y2)
  }
}


# EXPECT-TRUE q_quasigroup_total : Latin-square division is TOTAL on the quasigroup family (design s3; Fix-A2).
#   The division sub-family, Quasigroup rung (design s3; 02_algebra_tower.md s1 QUASIGROUP/LOOP - fully
#   ABSENT in Helios, grep zero) - SYN, cited standard math. q_quasigroup_division / fnd:QuasigroupDivisionShape
#   enforce only the UNIQUENESS half of the Latin-square law (no row/column repeats a result); a PARTIAL
#   division table where some equation a.x=b has NO solution x satisfies uniqueness vacuously and passed GREEN.
#   A quasigroup Cayley table must be a Latin square: division TOTAL (every a,b has a solution) AND UNIQUE.
#   This tooth adds the EXISTENCE half over the fnd:Quasigroup FAMILY (fnd:quasigroupModel AND - via
#   fnd:Loop rdfs:subClassOf fnd:Quasigroup - fnd:loopModel): for every ?qg a fnd:Quasigroup and every pair
#   of carrier elements (a,b) - the carrier DERIVED as the elements appearing as a fnd:opLeft of some row of
#   ?qg (in a Latin square every element is some left operand, so this is exact) - there is a LEFT-division
#   solution x with a.x=b AND a RIGHT-division solution y with y.a=b.
#   DATA CONTRACT (algebra_spine.ttl): at least one op row over some ?qg a fnd:Quasigroup exists (non-vacuity
#     anchor, FALSE on the empty graph - the 9-row cyclic Z/3 Latin square AND the 25-row order-5 loop Latin
#     square, both TOTAL); for EVERY ?qg a fnd:Quasigroup and every pair (a,b) of its carrier elements, EXISTS
#     x with a.x=b (left-division totality) AND EXISTS y with y.a=b (right-division totality). The ?qg a
#     fnd:Quasigroup guard is essential - without it the non-Latin fnd:semigroupModel / fnd:monoidModel rows
#     would be misread as partial-division tables.
#   PROBE OF RECORD (must flip True->False, mirrored by fnd:QuasigroupTotalityShape): DELETE the row
#     fnd:appQgAC (A.C=C) from fnd:quasigroupModel, so the A-row becomes {A.A=A, A.B=B} and A.x never reaches
#     C - the pair (a=A, b=C) has no left-division solution, the left-totality inner FILTER NOT EXISTS finds
#     it, and the ASK is FALSE (while q_quasigroup_division stays TRUE - a deleted row adds no duplicate).
PREFIX fnd: <urn:silmaril:fnd:#>
ASK {
  ?anchor fnd:opStructure ?qg0 . ?qg0 a fnd:Quasigroup .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?qg a fnd:Quasigroup .
    ?ra fnd:opStructure ?qg ; fnd:opLeft ?a .
    ?rb fnd:opStructure ?qg ; fnd:opLeft ?b .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?rx fnd:opStructure ?qg ; fnd:opLeft ?a ; fnd:opRight ?x ; fnd:opResult ?b }
  }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?qg2 a fnd:Quasigroup .
    ?ra2 fnd:opStructure ?qg2 ; fnd:opLeft ?a2 .
    ?rb2 fnd:opStructure ?qg2 ; fnd:opLeft ?b2 .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?ry fnd:opStructure ?qg2 ; fnd:opLeft ?y ; fnd:opRight ?a2 ; fnd:opResult ?b2 }
  }
}


# EXPECT-TRUE q_loop_identity : the two-sided identity holds on every fnd:Loop witness (design s3; L1 close).
#   The division sub-family, Loop rung (design s3; 02_algebra_tower.md s1 QUASIGROUP/LOOP - fully ABSENT in
#   Helios, grep zero) - SYN, cited standard math. A loop is a fnd:Quasigroup (Latin-square division) that
#   ALSO has a two-sided identity e (e.x=x, x.e=x for all x); a quasigroup that is associative is a group, so
#   a genuine loop is chosen NON-ASSOCIATIVE (order 5 is the smallest such). The Loop rung is a fnd:Quasigroup
#   + this one ADDED law (fnd:lawIdentity, fnd:addsLaw), minted as a fnd:PresentedAlgebra. This is the DISTINCT
#   per-rung tooth for fnd:Loop's added law, at parity with every sibling rung (a SYN witness fnd:loopModel +
#   this biting tooth), symmetric to q_abelian_comm re-adding commutativity over a distinct witness. It closes
#   the L1 hole: the lone identity tooth q_monoid_identity anchors on fnd:hasIdentityElement subjects, so an
#   identity-LESS loop was never checked and passed vacuously. This tooth makes 'every fnd:Loop carries a
#   two-sided identity' a CHECKABLE graph fact: a fnd:Loop with NO identity element, or whose declared identity
#   fails the unit law, is RED.
#   DATA CONTRACT (algebra_spine.ttl): at least one fnd:Loop exists (non-vacuity anchor, FALSE on the empty
#     graph - fnd:loopModel a fnd:Loop, fnd:hasIdentityElement fnd:elemE, with the 25-row order-5 Latin-square
#     table whose E-row E.x=x and E-column x.E=x for all x in {E,A,B,C,D}); EVERY fnd:Loop carries a
#     fnd:hasIdentityElement (EXISTENCE), and for every fnd:Loop with declared identity ?e, NO op row with ?e
#     on the left has a result != its right operand and NO row with ?e on the right has a result != its left
#     operand (GENUINENESS of the two-sided unit).
#   PROBE OF RECORD (must flip True->False, mirrored by fnd:LoopIdentityShape): a fnd:Loop that is a quasigroup
#     with NO fnd:hasIdentityElement (fnd:probeLoopNoIdentity, a genuine 3-element Latin square with no unit) -
#     the EXISTENCE clause finds a loop lacking an identity, and the ASK is FALSE.
PREFIX fnd: <urn:silmaril:fnd:#>
ASK {
  ?l0 a fnd:Loop .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?l a fnd:Loop .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?l fnd:hasIdentityElement ?e0 }
  }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?lm a fnd:Loop ; fnd:hasIdentityElement ?e .
    {
      ?rL fnd:opStructure ?lm ; fnd:opLeft ?e ; fnd:opRight ?x ; fnd:opResult ?rLr .
      FILTER(?rLr != ?x)
    } UNION {
      ?rR fnd:opStructure ?lm ; fnd:opLeft ?x ; fnd:opRight ?e ; fnd:opResult ?rRr .
      FILTER(?rRr != ?x)
    }
  }
}


# EXPECT-TRUE q_monoid_is_endo : the Monoid rung IS a one-object category / F(X,X) (the Pillar-4 seam).
#   The interlock tooth (design s3 q_monoid_is_endo; s5 Pillar 4 seam) - LIFTED (DS): Helios authors
#   "a monoid is a one-object category" (helios/srcy/papers/21_ologs_and_typed_english/chapters/05_yoneda_
#   for_typed_english/sections/04_monoid_monad_yoneda_binders.tex:2,16-17, citing Joy of Cats "a monoid as
#   a one-object category at lines 1001-1014"; End_C(X) with product=composition, unit=id_X, :36-39;
#   endopath monoid M_X=Hom(X,X), 31/sections/01_thesis.tex:29-32). This is the SEAM to Pillar 4: the
#   Monoid rung F(X,X) = the endomorphism monoid of one object = Curry's functionality F applied to one
#   type (design s5; Curry F(X,X), forward to T7 fnd:Functionality). This tooth makes the seam a CHECKABLE
#   graph fact: a monoid recognized as a one-object category (fnd:monoidAsCategory) must have its monoid
#   identity element (fnd:hasIdentityElement) be EXACTLY that category's object-identity arrow
#   (fnd:objectIdentityArrow), an endomorphism X->X (the sole object's id_X).
#   DATA CONTRACT (algebra_spine.ttl): at least one fnd:monoidAsCategory edge exists (non-vacuity anchor,
#     FALSE on the empty graph - fnd:endoMonoidWitness fnd:monoidAsCategory fnd:oneObjectCat); and for
#     EVERY monoid ?mm with fnd:monoidAsCategory ?c and fnd:hasIdentityElement ?id, ?c fnd:objectIdentityArrow
#     ?id (the monoid identity IS the object identity arrow) and ?id fnd:endoDomain ?x, fnd:endoCodomain ?x
#     for the category's fnd:soleObject ?x (id is a genuine endomorphism X->X).
#   PROBE OF RECORD (must flip True->False, mirrored by fnd:MonoidIsEndoShape): change fnd:endoMonoidWitness
#     fnd:hasIdentityElement from fnd:idEndoX to fnd:elemA (a non-identity element that is not the object's
#     id_X endomorphism) - the monoid identity no longer coincides with id_X, the inner
#     "?c fnd:objectIdentityArrow ?id" fails, and the ASK is FALSE.
PREFIX fnd: <urn:silmaril:fnd:#>
ASK {
  ?m fnd:monoidAsCategory ?cat0 .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?mm fnd:monoidAsCategory ?c ; fnd:hasIdentityElement ?id .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS {
      ?c fnd:objectIdentityArrow ?id ; fnd:soleObject ?x .
      ?id fnd:endoDomain ?x ; fnd:endoCodomain ?x .
    }
  }
}


# EXPECT-TRUE q_ring_distrib : TWO-SIDED distributivity holds on EVERY fnd:Semiring (x·(y+z)=x·y+x·z AND (y+z)·x=y·x+z·x).
#   The two-operation line, Semiring rung (design s3; ledger/W2/algebra_foundation/02_algebra_tower.md s "RING /
#   FIELD / MODULE - SYNTHESIZE (absent as algebra)":134-136). Ring/field/module are FULLY ABSENT from
#   Helios as algebra ("No algebraic ring, field (only record-field), or module (only code-module)",
#   02_algebra_tower.md:135); "Semiring" appears only as a valuation-coefficient device in optimization,
#   never as an axiomatized ring/semiring rung with +/x distributivity axioms (32/chapters/14/...:331,367,
#   401,473,546; :132 "No +/x distributivity axioms"). So the whole two-operation line is SYN, cited
#   standard universal algebra (the Directive-19/20 precedent: math is fact and liftable, cite the source,
#   never pretend a Helios lift). DISTRIBUTIVITY is fnd:Semiring's OWN added law (fnd:Semiring fnd:addsLaw
#   fnd:lawDistributivity, algebra_rings.ttl:490; fnd:satisfiesLaw :497), NOT a law of the strict subclass
#   fnd:Ring (which adds fnd:lawAdditiveInverse); so this tooth quantifies over the class where the law is
#   ADDED, fnd:Semiring - broadening the earlier fnd:Ring anchor that let a fresh, correctly-typed bare
#   fnd:Semiring with a non-distributive reified table pass GREEN (the sub-population-enforcement escape:
#   the defining law of a rung enforced only on a proper subclass). Each rung is minted as a
#   fnd:PresentedAlgebra through the LIFTED engine. CLASS-GENERAL + COMPLETE-LAW: this tooth makes the FULL
#   TWO-SIDED distributivity law a CHECKABLE graph fact over EVERY fnd:Semiring instance
#   (rdf:type/rdfs:subClassOf* fnd:Semiring - the raw-graph property path reaching fnd:ringModel AND
#   fnd:fieldModel, both fnd:Semiring since fnd:Ring subClassOf fnd:Semiring and fnd:Field subClassOf fnd:Ring,
#   plus any bare fnd:Semiring), for both sides: LEFT x·(y+z) = x·y + x·z AND RIGHT (y+z)·x = y·x + z·x.
#   The earlier witness-pinned form checked only LEFT distributivity over the single fnd:ringModel, arguing
#   "commutativity of GF(3) makes right follow" - a witness-specific escape a fresh non-commutative left-only
#   structure would slip through; right distributivity does NOT follow from left in a non-commutative semiring,
#   so BOTH sides are required (W-SP0-B). It is the two-operation analogue of q_semigroup_assoc one file up.
#   DATA CONTRACT (algebra_rings.ttl): at least one two-operation row exists on some ?m a fnd:Semiring (non-vacuity
#     anchor, FALSE on the empty graph - the full GF(3) + and x tables 0+0=0..2+2=1 and 0·0=0..2·2=1 over
#     fnd:ringModel/fnd:fieldModel, both fnd:Semiring); and NO triple (x,y,z) over ANY fnd:Semiring-typed model
#     has x·(y+z) != (x·y)+(x·z) OR (y+z)·x != (y·x)+(z·x).
#   PROBE OF RECORD (must flip True->False, mirrored by fnd:RingDistribShape): change the multiplicative row
#     fnd:appRingMul_1_2 (1·2) fnd:ringResult from fnd:ringTwo to fnd:ringOne (so for the triple (1,1,1):
#     x·(y+z) = 1·(1+1) = 1·2 = 1 while (x·y)+(x·z) = (1·1)+(1·1) = 1+1 = 2) - the inner LEFT EXISTS finds the
#     non-distributive triple, and the ASK is FALSE; a symmetric perturbation of an s·x row flips the RIGHT
#     clause; a FRESH non-distributive bare fnd:Semiring instance (grounding at fnd:Semiring, not fnd:Ring)
#     flips it the same way (class-general over the class where the law is added, complete law).
PREFIX rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
PREFIX fnd: <urn:silmaril:fnd:#>
ASK {
  ?mAnchor rdf:type/rdfs:subClassOf* fnd:Semiring .
  ?anchor fnd:ringStructure ?mAnchor ; fnd:ringOp fnd:additiveOp ; fnd:ringLeft ?la ; fnd:ringRight ?ra ; fnd:ringResult ?resa .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?ml rdf:type/rdfs:subClassOf* fnd:Semiring .
    ?ayz fnd:ringStructure ?ml ; fnd:ringOp fnd:additiveOp ; fnd:ringLeft ?y ; fnd:ringRight ?z ; fnd:ringResult ?s .
    ?mxs fnd:ringStructure ?ml ; fnd:ringOp fnd:multiplicativeOp ; fnd:ringLeft ?x ; fnd:ringRight ?s ; fnd:ringResult ?lft .
    ?mxy fnd:ringStructure ?ml ; fnd:ringOp fnd:multiplicativeOp ; fnd:ringLeft ?x ; fnd:ringRight ?y ; fnd:ringResult ?p .
    ?mxz fnd:ringStructure ?ml ; fnd:ringOp fnd:multiplicativeOp ; fnd:ringLeft ?x ; fnd:ringRight ?z ; fnd:ringResult ?q .
    ?apq fnd:ringStructure ?ml ; fnd:ringOp fnd:additiveOp ; fnd:ringLeft ?p ; fnd:ringRight ?q ; fnd:ringResult ?rgt .
    FILTER(?lft != ?rgt)
  }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?mr rdf:type/rdfs:subClassOf* fnd:Semiring .
    ?ayz2 fnd:ringStructure ?mr ; fnd:ringOp fnd:additiveOp ; fnd:ringLeft ?y2 ; fnd:ringRight ?z2 ; fnd:ringResult ?s2 .
    ?msx fnd:ringStructure ?mr ; fnd:ringOp fnd:multiplicativeOp ; fnd:ringLeft ?s2 ; fnd:ringRight ?x2 ; fnd:ringResult ?lft2 .
    ?myx fnd:ringStructure ?mr ; fnd:ringOp fnd:multiplicativeOp ; fnd:ringLeft ?y2 ; fnd:ringRight ?x2 ; fnd:ringResult ?p2 .
    ?mzx fnd:ringStructure ?mr ; fnd:ringOp fnd:multiplicativeOp ; fnd:ringLeft ?z2 ; fnd:ringRight ?x2 ; fnd:ringResult ?q2 .
    ?apq2 fnd:ringStructure ?mr ; fnd:ringOp fnd:additiveOp ; fnd:ringLeft ?p2 ; fnd:ringRight ?q2 ; fnd:ringResult ?rgt2 .
    FILTER(?lft2 != ?rgt2)
  }
}


# EXPECT-TRUE q_ring_add_assoc : additive ASSOCIATIVITY holds on every fnd:Semiring ((a+b)+c = a+(b+c)) (Fix-A1).
#   The two-operation line (design s3; 02_algebra_tower.md:134-136 - ring FULLY ABSENT as algebra in Helios).
#   SYN, cited standard ring theory. The Semiring->Ring->Field additive operation (+) must be ASSOCIATIVE
#   because a ring's additive part is an abelian GROUP and a semiring's a commutative MONOID; but the ring
#   reifies its operations via fnd:ringStructure/fnd:ringOp/fnd:ringLeft/fnd:ringRight/fnd:ringResult - a
#   DISTINCT vocabulary from the one-operation spine's fnd:opStructure that q_semigroup_assoc walks - so the
#   spine associativity tooth NEVER reached the ring additive operation: a fnd:Ring/fnd:Semiring with a
#   non-associative reified additive table passed GREEN (the Fix-A1 hole). This tooth closes it CLASS-GENERAL
#   over every fnd:Semiring (rdf:type/rdfs:subClassOf* fnd:Semiring, reaching fnd:ringModel and fnd:fieldModel).
#   DATA CONTRACT (algebra_rings.ttl): at least one additive row over some ?m a fnd:Semiring (non-vacuity
#     anchor, FALSE on the empty graph - the full GF(3) additive table 0+0=0..2+2=1 over fnd:ringModel); NO
#     triple (a,b,c) over ANY fnd:Semiring-typed model has (a+b)+c != a+(b+c).
#   PROBE OF RECORD (must flip True->False, mirrored by fnd:RingAddAssocShape): change fnd:appRingAdd_2_2 (2+2)
#     fnd:ringResult from fnd:ringOne to fnd:ringZero, so for (a,b,c)=(2,2,1): (a+b)+c = (2+2)+1 = 0+1 = 1
#     while a+(b+c) = 2+(2+1) = 2+0 = 2 - the inner EXISTS finds the non-associative triple, and the ASK is FALSE.
PREFIX rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
PREFIX fnd: <urn:silmaril:fnd:#>
ASK {
  ?mAnchor rdf:type/rdfs:subClassOf* fnd:Semiring .
  ?anchor fnd:ringStructure ?mAnchor ; fnd:ringOp fnd:additiveOp ; fnd:ringLeft ?la ; fnd:ringRight ?ra ; fnd:ringResult ?resa .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?m rdf:type/rdfs:subClassOf* fnd:Semiring .
    ?rab fnd:ringStructure ?m ; fnd:ringOp fnd:additiveOp ; fnd:ringLeft ?a ; fnd:ringRight ?b ; fnd:ringResult ?ab .
    ?rabc fnd:ringStructure ?m ; fnd:ringOp fnd:additiveOp ; fnd:ringLeft ?ab ; fnd:ringRight ?c ; fnd:ringResult ?lhs .
    ?rbc fnd:ringStructure ?m ; fnd:ringOp fnd:additiveOp ; fnd:ringLeft ?b ; fnd:ringRight ?c ; fnd:ringResult ?bc .
    ?rabc2 fnd:ringStructure ?m ; fnd:ringOp fnd:additiveOp ; fnd:ringLeft ?a ; fnd:ringRight ?bc ; fnd:ringResult ?rhs .
    FILTER(?lhs != ?rhs)
  }
}


# EXPECT-TRUE q_ring_add_comm : additive COMMUTATIVITY holds on every fnd:Semiring (a+b = b+a) (Fix-A1).
#   The two-operation line (design s3; 02_algebra_tower.md:134-136 - ring FULLY ABSENT as algebra in Helios).
#   SYN, cited standard ring theory. The Semiring->Ring->Field additive operation (+) must COMMUTE because a
#   semiring's additive part is a COMMUTATIVE monoid and a ring's an ABELIAN group; but the ring reifies via
#   fnd:ringStructure - DISTINCT from the spine fnd:opStructure that q_commmonoid_comm / q_abelian_comm walk -
#   so no spine commutativity tooth reached the ring additive operation: a fnd:Semiring/fnd:Ring with a
#   non-commutative reified additive table passed GREEN (the Fix-A1 hole). This tooth closes it CLASS-GENERAL
#   over every fnd:Semiring (rdf:type/rdfs:subClassOf* fnd:Semiring, reaching fnd:ringModel and fnd:fieldModel).
#   DATA CONTRACT (algebra_rings.ttl): at least one additive row over some ?m a fnd:Semiring (non-vacuity
#     anchor, FALSE on the empty graph - the full GF(3) additive table over fnd:ringModel); NO pair (a,b) over
#     ANY fnd:Semiring-typed model has a+b != b+a.
#   PROBE OF RECORD (must flip True->False, mirrored by fnd:RingAddCommShape): change fnd:appRingAdd_0_2 (0+2)
#     fnd:ringResult from fnd:ringTwo to fnd:ringZero, so 0+2 = 0 while 2+0 = 2 (fnd:appRingAdd_2_0) - the
#     pair (0,2) is non-commutative, the inner EXISTS finds it, and the ASK is FALSE.
PREFIX rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
PREFIX fnd: <urn:silmaril:fnd:#>
ASK {
  ?mAnchor rdf:type/rdfs:subClassOf* fnd:Semiring .
  ?anchor fnd:ringStructure ?mAnchor ; fnd:ringOp fnd:additiveOp ; fnd:ringLeft ?la ; fnd:ringRight ?ra ; fnd:ringResult ?resa .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?m rdf:type/rdfs:subClassOf* fnd:Semiring .
    ?rab fnd:ringStructure ?m ; fnd:ringOp fnd:additiveOp ; fnd:ringLeft ?a ; fnd:ringRight ?b ; fnd:ringResult ?ab .
    ?rba fnd:ringStructure ?m ; fnd:ringOp fnd:additiveOp ; fnd:ringLeft ?b ; fnd:ringRight ?a ; fnd:ringResult ?ba .
    FILTER(?ab != ?ba)
  }
}


# EXPECT-TRUE q_ring_mult_assoc : multiplicative ASSOCIATIVITY holds on every fnd:Semiring ((a*b)*c = a*(b*c)) (Fix-A1).
#   The two-operation line (design s3; 02_algebra_tower.md:134-136 - ring FULLY ABSENT as algebra in Helios).
#   SYN, cited standard ring theory. The Semiring->Ring->Field multiplicative operation (*) must be ASSOCIATIVE
#   because its multiplicative part is a MONOID (at minimum a semigroup); but the ring reifies via
#   fnd:ringStructure - DISTINCT from the spine fnd:opStructure that q_semigroup_assoc walks - so the spine
#   associativity tooth NEVER reached the ring multiplicative operation: a fnd:Ring/fnd:Semiring with a
#   non-associative reified multiplicative table passed GREEN (the Fix-A1 hole). This tooth closes it
#   CLASS-GENERAL over every fnd:Semiring (rdf:type/rdfs:subClassOf* fnd:Semiring, reaching fnd:ringModel and
#   fnd:fieldModel), mirroring q_ring_add_assoc over the fnd:multiplicativeOp rows.
#   DATA CONTRACT (algebra_rings.ttl): at least one multiplicative row over some ?m a fnd:Semiring (non-vacuity
#     anchor, FALSE on the empty graph - the full GF(3) multiplicative table 0*0=0..2*2=1 over fnd:ringModel);
#     NO triple (a,b,c) over ANY fnd:Semiring-typed model has (a*b)*c != a*(b*c).
#   PROBE OF RECORD (must flip True->False, mirrored by fnd:RingMultAssocShape): change fnd:appRingMul_2_1 (2*1)
#     fnd:ringResult from fnd:ringTwo to fnd:ringZero, so for (a,b,c)=(2,1,2): (a*b)*c = (2*1)*2 = 0*2 = 0
#     while a*(b*c) = 2*(1*2) = 2*2 = 1 - the inner EXISTS finds the non-associative triple, and the ASK is FALSE.
PREFIX rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
PREFIX fnd: <urn:silmaril:fnd:#>
ASK {
  ?mAnchor rdf:type/rdfs:subClassOf* fnd:Semiring .
  ?anchor fnd:ringStructure ?mAnchor ; fnd:ringOp fnd:multiplicativeOp ; fnd:ringLeft ?la ; fnd:ringRight ?ra ; fnd:ringResult ?resa .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?m rdf:type/rdfs:subClassOf* fnd:Semiring .
    ?rab fnd:ringStructure ?m ; fnd:ringOp fnd:multiplicativeOp ; fnd:ringLeft ?a ; fnd:ringRight ?b ; fnd:ringResult ?ab .
    ?rabc fnd:ringStructure ?m ; fnd:ringOp fnd:multiplicativeOp ; fnd:ringLeft ?ab ; fnd:ringRight ?c ; fnd:ringResult ?lhs .
    ?rbc fnd:ringStructure ?m ; fnd:ringOp fnd:multiplicativeOp ; fnd:ringLeft ?b ; fnd:ringRight ?c ; fnd:ringResult ?bc .
    ?rabc2 fnd:ringStructure ?m ; fnd:ringOp fnd:multiplicativeOp ; fnd:ringLeft ?a ; fnd:ringRight ?bc ; fnd:ringResult ?rhs .
    FILTER(?lhs != ?rhs)
  }
}


# EXPECT-TRUE q_ring_additive_inverse : every fnd:Ring element has a two-sided additive inverse (W1a).
#   The two-operation line, Ring rung (design s3; 02_algebra_tower.md:134-136 - ring FULLY ABSENT as algebra
#   in Helios). SYN, cited standard ring theory. fnd:Ring's SOLE added law over fnd:Semiring is
#   fnd:lawAdditiveInverse (the additive monoid (S,+,0) upgraded to an abelian group: every x has -x with
#   x+(-x)=0), which previously had NO tooth - the ring-family teeth checked only distributivity (Semiring)
#   and multiplicative inverse (Field), so a semiring-with-no-additive-inverse typed fnd:Ring passed GREEN.
#   This tooth is the ADDITIVE analogue of q_field_mult_inverse, reusing the genuine-inverse discipline over
#   the reified fnd:additiveOp table of a ring/field witness (a claimed additive-inverse fnd:AdditiveInversePairing
#   is GENUINE only if x+y=0 AND y+x=0), AND requiring EVERY fnd:hasRingElement of a fnd:Ring to carry such a
#   pairing (completeness). fnd:ringModel and fnd:fieldModel (GF(3); Field rdfs:subClassOf Ring) each have
#   inverses 0<->0, 1<->2, 2<->1.
#   DATA CONTRACT (algebra_rings.ttl): at least one fnd:AdditiveInversePairing exists (non-vacuity anchor,
#     FALSE on the empty graph - fnd:aipRingOne pairs 1 with 2 in fnd:ringModel, fnd:aipFieldOne 1 with 2 in
#     fnd:fieldModel, with the additive rows 1+2=0 and 2+1=0); for EVERY fnd:AdditiveInversePairing (model
#     ?rng, element ?x, inverse ?y) BOTH ?x+?y = 0 AND ?y+?x = 0 hold; AND EVERY fnd:hasRingElement of a
#     fnd:Ring carries a fnd:AdditiveInversePairing with it as fnd:aipElement.
#   PROBE OF RECORD (must flip True->False, mirrored by fnd:RingAdditiveInverseShape): a Boolean-OR 'ring' on
#     {0,1} with additive table 1+1=1 (so nothing + 1 = 0 and element 1 has NO additive inverse), carrying an
#     fnd:AdditiveInversePairing only for 0 - the completeness FILTER NOT EXISTS finds element 1 with no
#     pairing, and the ASK is FALSE (a semiring-with-no-additive-inverse masquerading as a ring).
PREFIX rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
PREFIX fnd: <urn:silmaril:fnd:#>
ASK {
  ?p0 a fnd:AdditiveInversePairing .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?pp a fnd:AdditiveInversePairing ; fnd:aipModel ?rng ; fnd:aipElement ?x ; fnd:aipInverse ?y .
    ?rng fnd:hasZeroElement ?zero .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS {
      ?xy fnd:ringStructure ?rng ; fnd:ringOp fnd:additiveOp ; fnd:ringLeft ?x ; fnd:ringRight ?y ; fnd:ringResult ?zero .
      ?yx fnd:ringStructure ?rng ; fnd:ringOp fnd:additiveOp ; fnd:ringLeft ?y ; fnd:ringRight ?x ; fnd:ringResult ?zero .
    }
  }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?rng2 a fnd:Ring ; fnd:hasRingElement ?e .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?q2 a fnd:AdditiveInversePairing ; fnd:aipModel ?rng2 ; fnd:aipElement ?e }
  }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?rngC rdf:type/rdfs:subClassOf* fnd:Ring .
    { ?rngC rdf:type/rdfs:subClassOf* fnd:Ring . FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?rngC fnd:hasRingElement ?re } }
    UNION
    { ?rngC rdf:type/rdfs:subClassOf* fnd:Ring . FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?rngC fnd:hasZeroElement ?rz } }
  }
}


# EXPECT-TRUE q_field_mult_inverse : every nonzero field element is multiplicatively invertible.
#   The two-operation line, Field rung (design s3; 02_algebra_tower.md "RING / FIELD / MODULE - SYNTHESIZE
#   (absent as algebra)":134-136 - field is FULLY ABSENT as algebra in Helios, only record-`field` hits). SYN,
#   cited standard field theory. The Field rung is a fnd:Ring + this one added law (fnd:lawMultInverse,
#   fnd:addsLaw): every element x != 0 has a two-sided multiplicative inverse x^-1 with x·x^-1 = 1. This tooth
#   reuses the SP2/T4 genuine-inverse discipline (a claimed inverse that does not undo -> RED, aob:retracts /
#   fnd:GroupInverseShape) at the MULTIPLICATIVE level, over the field witness fnd:fieldModel (GF(3) = {0,1,2}
#   with fnd:hasZeroElement 0 and fnd:hasOneElement 1): a claimed multiplicative-inverse pairing
#   (fnd:MultInversePairing: element x, inverse y in a field with one-element 1) is GENUINE only if x·y = 1
#   AND y·x = 1, AND every nonzero field element carries such a pairing. In GF(3): 1^-1 = 1 (1·1=1) and
#   2^-1 = 2 (2·2 = 4 = 1). It is the two-operation analogue of q_group_inverse.
#   DATA CONTRACT (algebra_rings.ttl): at least one fnd:MultInversePairing exists (non-vacuity anchor, FALSE
#     on the empty graph - fnd:mipPairOne pairs 1 with 1, fnd:mipPairTwo pairs 2 with 2, over fnd:fieldModel
#     whose fnd:hasOneElement is fnd:fieldOne, with the multiplicative rows 1·1=1 and 2·2=1); for EVERY
#     fnd:MultInversePairing (model ?fld, element ?x, inverse ?y) BOTH ?x·?y = 1 AND ?y·?x = 1 hold; AND EVERY
#     nonzero fnd:hasRingElement of a fnd:Field (an element != its fnd:hasZeroElement) carries a
#     fnd:MultInversePairing with it as fnd:mipElement.
#   PROBE OF RECORD (must flip True->False, mirrored by fnd:FieldMultInverseShape): change the multiplicative
#     row fnd:appFieldMul_2_2 (2·2) fnd:ringResult from fnd:fieldOne to fnd:fieldTwo (so 2·2 = 2 != 1) - the
#     claimed inverse 2 of 2 no longer multiplies to the field's one, the inner two-sided-undo FILTER NOT
#     EXISTS fails for fnd:mipPairTwo, and the ASK is FALSE (a "field" with a non-invertible nonzero element).
PREFIX fnd: <urn:silmaril:fnd:#>
ASK {
  ?p0 a fnd:MultInversePairing .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?pp a fnd:MultInversePairing ; fnd:mipModel ?fld ; fnd:mipElement ?x ; fnd:mipInverse ?y .
    ?fld fnd:hasOneElement ?one .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS {
      ?xy fnd:ringStructure ?fld ; fnd:ringOp fnd:multiplicativeOp ; fnd:ringLeft ?x ; fnd:ringRight ?y ; fnd:ringResult ?one .
      ?yx fnd:ringStructure ?fld ; fnd:ringOp fnd:multiplicativeOp ; fnd:ringLeft ?y ; fnd:ringRight ?x ; fnd:ringResult ?one .
    }
  }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?fld2 a fnd:Field ; fnd:hasRingElement ?e ; fnd:hasZeroElement ?zero .
    FILTER(?e != ?zero)
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?q2 a fnd:MultInversePairing ; fnd:mipModel ?fld2 ; fnd:mipElement ?e }
  }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?fldC a fnd:Field .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?fldC fnd:hasOneElement ?one }
  }
}


# EXPECT-TRUE q_module_scalar : the scalar action is well typed on the module witness (R x M -> M).
#   The algebra-space seam, Module rung (design s3; 02_algebra_tower.md "RING / FIELD / MODULE - SYNTHESIZE
#   (absent as algebra)":134-136 - module is FULLY ABSENT as algebra in Helios, only code-`module` hits). SYN,
#   cited standard module theory. The Module rung is a fnd:AlgebraicStructure child (an abelian group of
#   vectors + a ring acting by scalars) adding one law (fnd:lawScalarAction, fnd:addsLaw), minted as a
#   fnd:PresentedAlgebra. This tooth makes the scalar action's TYPING a CHECKABLE graph fact (the same
#   edge-existence discipline as q_membership_typed / q_set_carrier): a module fnd:moduleOverRing a base ring,
#   with vectors enumerated by fnd:hasModuleVector, and a reified scalar action (fnd:ScalarAction:
#   fnd:saModule the module, fnd:saScalar r, fnd:saVector m, fnd:saResult r·m) is well typed only when the
#   scalar r is a fnd:hasRingElement of the base ring AND the result r·m is a fnd:hasModuleVector of the module
#   (the action lands back in the module, R x M -> M). The witness fnd:moduleModel is the rank-1 free module
#   {V0,V1,V2} over the ring GF(3), with 1·V1=V1, 2·V1=V2, 2·V2=V1.
#   DATA CONTRACT (algebra_rings.ttl): at least one ?a a fnd:ScalarAction exists (non-vacuity anchor, FALSE on
#     the empty graph - fnd:saOneV1 / fnd:saTwoV1 / fnd:saTwoV2 over fnd:moduleModel, and fnd:saUnitLaw over
#     fnd:vectorSpaceModel); and EVERY fnd:ScalarAction (module ?m over ring ?ring, scalar ?r, result ?res)
#     has ?ring fnd:hasRingElement ?r AND ?m fnd:hasModuleVector ?res (the action is well typed).
#   PROBE OF RECORD (must flip True->False, mirrored by fnd:ModuleScalarShape): inject an escaping action -
#     fnd:probeEscapingScalarAction a fnd:ScalarAction ; fnd:saModule fnd:moduleModel ; fnd:saScalar
#     fnd:ringOne ; fnd:saVector fnd:vecV1 ; fnd:saResult fnd:ringZero (a result that is a RING element, not a
#     fnd:hasModuleVector of the module - the action escapes M) - the inner typing FILTER NOT EXISTS fails and
#     the ASK is FALSE.
PREFIX fnd: <urn:silmaril:fnd:#>
ASK {
  ?a0 a fnd:ScalarAction .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?sa a fnd:ScalarAction ; fnd:saModule ?m ; fnd:saScalar ?r ; fnd:saResult ?res .
    ?m fnd:moduleOverRing ?ring .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS {
      ?ring fnd:hasRingElement ?r .
      ?m fnd:hasModuleVector ?res .
    }
  }
}


# EXPECT-TRUE q_module_scalar_law : the FULL module scalar-action law holds on EVERY fnd:Module (W-SP0-B).
#   The algebra-space seam, Module rung (design s3; 02_algebra_tower.md:134-136 - module FULLY ABSENT as
#   algebra in Helios). SYN, cited standard module theory. q_module_scalar checks only the action's TYPING
#   (R x M -> M); this tooth COMPLETES the module law fnd:lawScalarAction, whose equationBody is exactly
#   "1.m = m ; (r.s).m = r.(s.m) ; r.(m+n) = r.m + r.n ; (r+s).m = r.m + s.m" - so a well-typed but
#   NON-UNITAL / non-scalar-associative / non-bi-distributive module no longer passes GREEN (the
#   sub-clause-only-law defect the hostile review keeps finding variants of). CLASS-GENERAL: QUANTIFIES OVER
#   EVERY fnd:Module via rdf:type/rdfs:subClassOf* fnd:Module (raw-graph property path reaching the plain
#   module fnd:moduleModel AND the vector space fnd:vectorSpaceModel, a fnd:VectorSpace subClassOf fnd:Module);
#   the SHACL fnd:ModuleScalarLawShape does the same under inference=rdfs.
#   DATA CONTRACT (algebra_rings.ttl): at least one fnd:ScalarAction exists on some ?m a fnd:Module
#     (non-vacuity anchor, FALSE on the empty graph); and over EVERY fnd:Module: (1) UNITALITY - no action
#     whose scalar is the base ring's fnd:hasOneElement has result != vector (1.m=m); (2) SCALAR-ASSOCIATIVITY
#     - no base-ring product r.s=c gives c.m != r.(s.m); (3) LEFT BI-DISTRIBUTIVITY - no vector sum m+n (over
#     the fnd:moduleAdditiveGroup) gives r.(m+n) != (r.m)+(r.n); (4) RIGHT BI-DISTRIBUTIVITY - no base-ring
#     sum r+s=c gives c.m != (r.m)+(s.m). fnd:moduleModel (over GF(3) fnd:ringModel, additive group
#     fnd:moduleAddGroup) and fnd:vectorSpaceModel (over fnd:fieldModel, additive group fnd:abelianModel)
#     satisfy all four.
#   PROBE OF RECORD (each flips True->False, mirrored by fnd:ModuleScalarLawShape's four constraints):
#     unitality - fnd:saOneV1 fnd:saResult -> fnd:vecV2 (1.V1=V2!=V1); scalar-assoc - fnd:saTwoV2 fnd:saResult
#     -> fnd:vecV0 ((2.2).V1=1.V1=V1 while 2.(2.V1)=2.V2=V0); left bi-distrib - fnd:appMAddV2V2 fnd:opResult
#     perturbed; right bi-distrib - fnd:appRingAdd_1_1 fnd:ringResult perturbed. A FRESH non-unital or
#     non-distributive fnd:Module instance flips it the same way (class-general, complete law).
PREFIX rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
PREFIX fnd: <urn:silmaril:fnd:#>
ASK {
  ?mAnchor rdf:type/rdfs:subClassOf* fnd:Module .
  ?aAnchor fnd:saModule ?mAnchor .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?m1 rdf:type/rdfs:subClassOf* fnd:Module ; fnd:moduleOverRing ?ring1 .
    ?ring1 fnd:hasOneElement ?one .
    ?u fnd:saModule ?m1 ; fnd:saScalar ?one ; fnd:saVector ?v ; fnd:saResult ?rv .
    FILTER(?rv != ?v)
  }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?m2 rdf:type/rdfs:subClassOf* fnd:Module ; fnd:moduleOverRing ?ring2 .
    ?rs fnd:ringStructure ?ring2 ; fnd:ringOp fnd:multiplicativeOp ; fnd:ringLeft ?r ; fnd:ringRight ?s ; fnd:ringResult ?c .
    ?cm fnd:saModule ?m2 ; fnd:saScalar ?c ; fnd:saVector ?mv ; fnd:saResult ?lhs .
    ?sm fnd:saModule ?m2 ; fnd:saScalar ?s ; fnd:saVector ?mv ; fnd:saResult ?w .
    ?rw fnd:saModule ?m2 ; fnd:saScalar ?r ; fnd:saVector ?w ; fnd:saResult ?rhs .
    FILTER(?lhs != ?rhs)
  }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?m3 rdf:type/rdfs:subClassOf* fnd:Module ; fnd:moduleAdditiveGroup ?g3 .
    ?smn fnd:opStructure ?g3 ; fnd:opLeft ?mm ; fnd:opRight ?nn ; fnd:opResult ?mn .
    ?rmn fnd:saModule ?m3 ; fnd:saScalar ?r3 ; fnd:saVector ?mn ; fnd:saResult ?lhs3 .
    ?rm fnd:saModule ?m3 ; fnd:saScalar ?r3 ; fnd:saVector ?mm ; fnd:saResult ?pm .
    ?rn fnd:saModule ?m3 ; fnd:saScalar ?r3 ; fnd:saVector ?nn ; fnd:saResult ?pn .
    ?sum3 fnd:opStructure ?g3 ; fnd:opLeft ?pm ; fnd:opRight ?pn ; fnd:opResult ?rhs3 .
    FILTER(?lhs3 != ?rhs3)
  }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?m4 rdf:type/rdfs:subClassOf* fnd:Module ; fnd:moduleOverRing ?ring4 ; fnd:moduleAdditiveGroup ?g4 .
    ?rs4 fnd:ringStructure ?ring4 ; fnd:ringOp fnd:additiveOp ; fnd:ringLeft ?r4 ; fnd:ringRight ?s4 ; fnd:ringResult ?c4 .
    ?cm4 fnd:saModule ?m4 ; fnd:saScalar ?c4 ; fnd:saVector ?mv4 ; fnd:saResult ?lhs4 .
    ?rm4 fnd:saModule ?m4 ; fnd:saScalar ?r4 ; fnd:saVector ?mv4 ; fnd:saResult ?pr4 .
    ?sm4 fnd:saModule ?m4 ; fnd:saScalar ?s4 ; fnd:saVector ?mv4 ; fnd:saResult ?ps4 .
    ?sum4 fnd:opStructure ?g4 ; fnd:opLeft ?pr4 ; fnd:opRight ?ps4 ; fnd:opResult ?rhs4 .
    FILTER(?lhs4 != ?rhs4)
  }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?mE rdf:type/rdfs:subClassOf* fnd:Module .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?aE fnd:saModule ?mE }
  }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?mU rdf:type/rdfs:subClassOf* fnd:Module ; fnd:moduleOverRing ?rU .
    ?rU fnd:hasOneElement ?oneU .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?aU fnd:saModule ?mU ; fnd:saScalar ?oneU }
  }
}


# EXPECT-TRUE q_vectorspace_axioms : the vector-space axioms hold over a fnd:Field (scalars a field + unit law).
#   The algebra-space seam, VectorSpace rung (design s3/s4; 02_algebra_tower.md:136 - vector spaces appear only
#   incidentally as "ambient vector spaces" in a sheaf-consistency operator, appendices/35/.../00_content.tex:504,
#   never a defined VectorSpace rung). SYN, cited standard linear algebra. A vector space is a fnd:Module whose
#   scalar ring is a FIELD; the VectorSpace rung is a fnd:Module + this one added law (fnd:lawFieldScalars,
#   fnd:addsLaw). Fully teeth-proving all 8 axioms by numeric table is out of scope (design s9: the teeth check
#   the distinguishing laws, not a proof assistant); this tooth makes the DISTINGUISHING vector-space content a
#   CHECKABLE graph fact - ALL EIGHT axioms bite (W2 close; the earlier 'axioms 6-8 inherited from
#   q_module_scalar + q_ring_distrib' claim was FALSE and is removed): axioms 1-4 ((V,+) abelian group) via
#   the fnd:vectorAdditiveGroup a fnd:AbelianGroup typing (commutativity teeth-proved by q_abelian_comm) plus
#   the fnd:scalarField a fnd:Field upgrade; axiom 5 (unit scalar 1v=v) via fnd:unitLawAction; axiom 6
#   (a(u+v)=au+av) via the scalar-over-vector-sum clause; axiom 7 ((a+b)v=av+bv) via the field-sum clause;
#   axiom 8 ((ab)v=a(bv)) via the field-product clause. The witness fnd:vectorSpaceModel has fnd:scalarField
#   fnd:fieldModel (GF(3)), fnd:vectorAdditiveGroup fnd:abelianModel ({E=0,A=1,B=2}, sums A+A=B / B+B=A),
#   fnd:unitLawAction fnd:saUnitLaw (1.A=A), and scalar actions 2.A=B / 2.B=A.
#   DATA CONTRACT (algebra_rings.ttl / algebra_spine.ttl): at least one ?vs a fnd:VectorSpace exists
#     (non-vacuity anchor, FALSE on the empty graph - fnd:vectorSpaceModel); EVERY fnd:VectorSpace has a
#     fnd:scalarField that is a fnd:Field AND a fnd:vectorAdditiveGroup that is a fnd:AbelianGroup; NO unit-law
#     action breaks 1.v=v; NO scalar a over a vector sum u+v breaks a(u+v)=au+av (axiom 6); NO field sum a+b
#     over v breaks (a+b)v=av+bv (axiom 7); NO field product ab over v breaks (ab)v=a(bv) (axiom 8).
#   PROBE OF RECORD (each flips True->False, mirrored by fnd:VectorSpaceAxiomsShape): (axiom 5) fnd:saUnitLaw
#     fnd:saResult fnd:elemA->fnd:elemB (1.A=B!=A); (axiom 6) fnd:appAbBB fnd:opResult fnd:elemA->fnd:elemE
#     (a(u+v)!=au+av on a=2,u=v=A); (axiom 7) fnd:appFieldAdd_1_1 fnd:ringResult fnd:fieldTwo->fnd:fieldOne
#     ((a+b)v!=av+bv on a=b=1,v=A); (axiom 8) fnd:appFieldMul_2_1 fnd:ringResult fnd:fieldTwo->fnd:fieldOne
#     ((ab)v!=a(bv) on a=2,b=1,v=A) - each makes the matching FILTER NOT EXISTS find a violating witness.
PREFIX fnd: <urn:silmaril:fnd:#>
ASK {
  ?vs0 a fnd:VectorSpace .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?vF a fnd:VectorSpace .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS {
      ?vF fnd:scalarField ?f . ?f fnd:hasOneElement ?fone . ?f fnd:hasZeroElement ?fzero .
      ?mp a fnd:MultInversePairing ; fnd:mipModel ?f .
    }
  }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?vG a fnd:VectorSpace .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS {
      ?vG fnd:vectorAdditiveGroup ?g . ?g fnd:hasIdentityElement ?gid .
      ?gp a fnd:InversePairing ; fnd:pairingModel ?g .
    }
  }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?v2 a fnd:VectorSpace ; fnd:scalarField ?f2 ; fnd:unitLawAction ?ula .
    ?f2 fnd:hasOneElement ?one .
    ?ula fnd:saScalar ?one ; fnd:saVector ?vec ; fnd:saResult ?r .
    FILTER(?r != ?vec)
  }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?v6 a fnd:VectorSpace ; fnd:vectorAdditiveGroup ?g6 .
    ?suv fnd:opStructure ?g6 ; fnd:opLeft ?u ; fnd:opRight ?vv ; fnd:opResult ?s .
    ?as6 fnd:saModule ?v6 ; fnd:saScalar ?a6 ; fnd:saVector ?s ; fnd:saResult ?lhs6 .
    ?au6 fnd:saModule ?v6 ; fnd:saScalar ?a6 ; fnd:saVector ?u ; fnd:saResult ?pu .
    ?av6 fnd:saModule ?v6 ; fnd:saScalar ?a6 ; fnd:saVector ?vv ; fnd:saResult ?pv .
    ?sum6 fnd:opStructure ?g6 ; fnd:opLeft ?pu ; fnd:opRight ?pv ; fnd:opResult ?rhs6 .
    FILTER(?lhs6 != ?rhs6)
  }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?v7 a fnd:VectorSpace ; fnd:vectorAdditiveGroup ?g7 ; fnd:scalarField ?fld7 .
    ?abr7 fnd:ringStructure ?fld7 ; fnd:ringOp fnd:additiveOp ; fnd:ringLeft ?a7 ; fnd:ringRight ?b7 ; fnd:ringResult ?c7 .
    ?cv7 fnd:saModule ?v7 ; fnd:saScalar ?c7 ; fnd:saVector ?vec7 ; fnd:saResult ?lhs7 .
    ?av7 fnd:saModule ?v7 ; fnd:saScalar ?a7 ; fnd:saVector ?vec7 ; fnd:saResult ?pa7 .
    ?bv7 fnd:saModule ?v7 ; fnd:saScalar ?b7 ; fnd:saVector ?vec7 ; fnd:saResult ?pb7 .
    ?sum7 fnd:opStructure ?g7 ; fnd:opLeft ?pa7 ; fnd:opRight ?pb7 ; fnd:opResult ?rhs7 .
    FILTER(?lhs7 != ?rhs7)
  }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?v8 a fnd:VectorSpace ; fnd:scalarField ?fld8 .
    ?abr8 fnd:ringStructure ?fld8 ; fnd:ringOp fnd:multiplicativeOp ; fnd:ringLeft ?a8 ; fnd:ringRight ?b8 ; fnd:ringResult ?c8 .
    ?cv8 fnd:saModule ?v8 ; fnd:saScalar ?c8 ; fnd:saVector ?vec8 ; fnd:saResult ?lhs8 .
    ?bv8 fnd:saModule ?v8 ; fnd:saScalar ?b8 ; fnd:saVector ?vec8 ; fnd:saResult ?w8 .
    ?aw8 fnd:saModule ?v8 ; fnd:saScalar ?a8 ; fnd:saVector ?w8 ; fnd:saResult ?rhs8 .
    FILTER(?lhs8 != ?rhs8)
  }
}


# =====================================================================================
# T6 — spaces.ttl EXPECT-TRUE ASKs (design s4; ledger/W2/algebra_foundation/04_space_constructs.md).
# The LIFTED site/sheaf core (q_sheaf_glues) + the SYN point-set spaces (q_topology_axioms,
# q_metric_triangle). q_vectorspace_axioms (T5) is SHARED with this pillar (design s4) and is not
# re-authored here. Each ASK is non-vacuous (FALSE on the pre-T6 graph) and mirrored by a SHACL tooth.
# =====================================================================================

# EXPECT-TRUE q_sheaf_glues : agreeing local sections glue to a unique global section (sheaf condition).
#   The LIFTED core space construct (design s4; 04_space_constructs.md s1.1 "the deepest genuine space"):
#   a fnd:Sheaf is a fnd:Presheaf F:C^op->Set satisfying the equalizer-form sheaf condition on a covering
#   family {U_i -> U} - F(U) is the equalizer of prod_i F(U_i) => prod_ij F(U_i cap U_j) (LIFTED verbatim
#   from helios/srcy/papers/19_mereology_as_colimit/chapters/05_atomic_colimit_constructions/sections/
#   02_sheaf_condition_for_part_of.tex:30-52, the equalizer diagram; the site-level descent extension lives
#   in paper 25, 25/01/00_...tex:30-90). The reified equalizer datum is a fnd:MatchingFamily: two local
#   sections (fnd:familyOverA / fnd:familyOverB) whose overlap restrictions (fnd:restrictionToOverlapA /
#   fnd:restrictionToOverlapB) AGREE, together with its unique gluing (fnd:hasGluing) restricting back to
#   both legs (fnd:glueRestrictsToA / fnd:glueRestrictsToB). The corpus's own honesty caveat is the
#   presheaf-as-function collapse (19/05/02:151-157): absent the equalizer, the apex is conjectured, not
#   constructed - so the tooth makes the equalizer (agreement -> unique glue) a graph fact.
#   DATA CONTRACT (spaces.ttl): at least one fnd:MatchingFamily exists (non-vacuity anchor, FALSE on the
#     pre-T6 graph - fnd:matchingFamilyWitness); EVERY matching family whose two overlap restrictions AGREE
#     (fnd:restrictionToOverlapA = fnd:restrictionToOverlapB) HAS a fnd:hasGluing that restricts to exactly
#     its two legs (fnd:glueRestrictsToA = fnd:familyOverA and fnd:glueRestrictsToB = fnd:familyOverB); and
#     NO matching family carries two DISTINCT fnd:hasGluing values (uniqueness of the amalgamation).
#   PROBE OF RECORD (must flip True->False, mirrored by fnd:SheafGluesShape): repoint fnd:secGlobal
#     fnd:glueRestrictsToA from fnd:secA to fnd:secB (the glue no longer restricts to the first leg) - the
#     agreeing family fnd:matchingFamilyWitness then has NO valid gluing, the inner EXISTS fails, and the
#     ASK is FALSE (local sections agreeing on overlaps with no unique glue -> RED).
PREFIX fnd: <urn:silmaril:fnd:#>
ASK {
  ?mf0 a fnd:MatchingFamily .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?mf a fnd:MatchingFamily ;
        fnd:restrictionToOverlapA ?ra ; fnd:restrictionToOverlapB ?rb ;
        fnd:familyOverA ?sa ; fnd:familyOverB ?sb .
    FILTER(?ra = ?rb)
    FILTER NOT EXISTS {
      ?mf fnd:hasGluing ?g .
      ?g fnd:glueRestrictsToA ?sa ; fnd:glueRestrictsToB ?sb .
    }
  }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?mf2 a fnd:MatchingFamily ; fnd:hasGluing ?g1 , ?g2 .
    FILTER(?g1 != ?g2)
  }
}

# EXPECT-TRUE q_topology_axioms : tau contains empty/X and is closed under finite intersection + union.
#   The SYN point-set topological space (design s4; 04_space_constructs.md s3, D2: the corpus REFUSES
#   point-set topology on its objects - 19/05/03_cell_complex_pasting.tex:11-13,69-74 "makes no claim about
#   a point-set topology on Mittens" - so fnd:TopologicalSpace is SYN, cited standard topology, NOT a
#   Helios lift; the genuine authored space is the fnd:Site). A fnd:TopologicalSpace (X,tau) must satisfy
#   the open-set axioms: tau contains the empty set and X, and is closed under finite intersection and
#   arbitrary union. The witness is the discrete topology on X={a,b}: tau={empty,{a},{b},{a,b}}. Closure
#   is reified as fnd:OpenIntersection / fnd:OpenUnion rows (fnd:intersectResult / fnd:unionResult), each
#   scoped to its space by fnd:intersectionIn / fnd:unionIn, so the closure axioms are checkable graph facts.
#   DATA CONTRACT (spaces.ttl): at least one fnd:TopologicalSpace exists (non-vacuity, FALSE pre-T6 -
#     fnd:topSpaceWitness); EVERY space has its fnd:hasEmptyOpen and fnd:hasTotalOpen both among its
#     fnd:hasOpenSet; NO reified fnd:OpenIntersection of two opens has a fnd:intersectResult that is not an
#     open; and NO reified fnd:OpenUnion of two opens has a fnd:unionResult that is not an open.
#   PROBE OF RECORD (must flip True->False, mirrored by fnd:TopologyAxiomsShape): repoint fnd:ixAB
#     (the reified {a} cap {b} = empty row) fnd:intersectResult from fnd:openEmpty to fnd:setNonOpen (a
#     fnd:Set that is NOT a fnd:hasOpenSet of the space) - tau is then not closed under finite intersection,
#     the intersection-closure clause fires, and the ASK is FALSE (tau not closed under intersection -> RED).
PREFIX fnd: <urn:silmaril:fnd:#>
ASK {
  ?ts0 a fnd:TopologicalSpace .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?ts a fnd:TopologicalSpace .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS {
      ?ts fnd:hasEmptyOpen ?e ; fnd:hasOpenSet ?e .
      ?ts fnd:hasTotalOpen ?x ; fnd:hasOpenSet ?x .
    }
  }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?ix a fnd:OpenIntersection ; fnd:intersectionIn ?ts2 ;
        fnd:intersectLeft ?l ; fnd:intersectRight ?r ; fnd:intersectResult ?res .
    ?ts2 fnd:hasOpenSet ?l , ?r .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?ts2 fnd:hasOpenSet ?res }
  }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?un a fnd:OpenUnion ; fnd:unionIn ?ts3 ;
        fnd:unionLeft ?ul ; fnd:unionRight ?ur ; fnd:unionResult ?ures .
    ?ts3 fnd:hasOpenSet ?ul , ?ur .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?ts3 fnd:hasOpenSet ?ures }
  }
}

# EXPECT-TRUE q_metric_triangle : d satisfies identity d(x,x)=0, identity of indiscernibles (d(x,y)=0 => x=y),
#   symmetry, and the triangle inequality.
#   The SYN point-set metric space (design s4; 04_space_constructs.md s1.4/D4: metric spaces are USAGE in
#   Helios - metric feature codomains (A_k, delta_k), the tessellation graph metric d_f^T - never an
#   axiomatized (X,d) atom, so fnd:MetricSpace is SYN, cited standard metric geometry). A fnd:MetricSpace
#   is enriched over the commutative monoid ([0,inf], >=, +) (D4: the Lawvere-enriched-category reading ties
#   the space pillar to the algebra pillar's fnd:CommutativeMonoid; fnd:enrichedOver). Distances are reified
#   as fnd:DistanceAssertion rows (fnd:distFrom / fnd:distTo / fnd:distValue, an xsd:decimal). The witness
#   is the 3-point space {A,B,C} with d(A,B)=d(B,C)=1, d(A,C)=2, self-distances 0.
#   DATA CONTRACT (spaces.ttl): at least one fnd:MetricSpace exists (non-vacuity, FALSE pre-T6 -
#     fnd:metricSpaceWitness); NO self-distance d(p,p) is nonzero (identity); NO two DISTINCT points x!=y
#     have d(x,y)=0 (identity of indiscernibles - the axiom separating a METRIC from a pseudometric); NO
#     pair has d(x,y) != d(y,x) (symmetry); and NO triple has d(x,z) > d(x,y) + d(y,z) (triangle inequality).
#   PROBE OF RECORD (must flip True->False, mirrored by fnd:MetricTriangleShape): (triangle) change fnd:distAC
#     (the d(A,C)=2 assertion) fnd:distValue from 2 to 5 - then d(A,C)=5 > d(A,B)+d(B,C)=2 -> FALSE; OR
#     (indiscernibles) type a pseudometric with two distinct zero-distance points d(x,y)=0, x!=y as a
#     fnd:MetricSpace - the identity-of-indiscernibles clause fires -> the ASK is FALSE (RED).
PREFIX fnd: <urn:silmaril:fnd:#>
ASK {
  ?ms0 a fnd:MetricSpace .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?ms a fnd:MetricSpace ; fnd:hasDistanceAssertion ?d .
    ?d fnd:distFrom ?p ; fnd:distTo ?p ; fnd:distValue ?v .
    FILTER(?v != 0)
  }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?msI a fnd:MetricSpace ; fnd:hasDistanceAssertion ?dI .
    ?dI fnd:distFrom ?a ; fnd:distTo ?b ; fnd:distValue ?vI .
    FILTER(?a != ?b && ?vI = 0)
  }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?ms2 a fnd:MetricSpace ; fnd:hasDistanceAssertion ?d1 , ?d2 .
    ?d1 fnd:distFrom ?x ; fnd:distTo ?y ; fnd:distValue ?v1 .
    ?d2 fnd:distFrom ?y ; fnd:distTo ?x ; fnd:distValue ?v2 .
    FILTER(?v1 != ?v2)
  }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?ms3 a fnd:MetricSpace ; fnd:hasDistanceAssertion ?dxz , ?dxy , ?dyz .
    ?dxz fnd:distFrom ?x2 ; fnd:distTo ?z2 ; fnd:distValue ?vxz .
    ?dxy fnd:distFrom ?x2 ; fnd:distTo ?y2 ; fnd:distValue ?vxy .
    ?dyz fnd:distFrom ?y2 ; fnd:distTo ?z2 ; fnd:distValue ?vyz .
    FILTER(?vxz > ?vxy + ?vyz)
  }
}


# =====================================================================================
# T7 — functionality.ttl EXPECT-TRUE ASKs (design s5, Pillar 4; Directive 19; H. B. Curry, First
# Properties of Functionality in Combinatory Logic, Tohoku Math. J. 41 (1936) 371-401, CITED not
# committed; ledger/W2/algebra_foundation/06_functionality_synthesis.md + 06b_curry_lift.md +
# 06c_sp1_functionality_reanchor.md). The arrow pillar: the Frame RECOGNIZED as Curry's F (not rebuilt),
# the F(dom,cod) variance bifunctor (contravariant domain / covariant codomain), and the Curry s6
# self-application paradox-quarantine. Each ASK is non-vacuous (FALSE on the pre-T7 graph) and mirrored
# by a SHACL tooth proven to bite under a probe of record.
# =====================================================================================

# EXPECT-TRUE q_frame_is_functionality : prim:Frame is recognized as Curry's functionality F (not rebuilt).
#   The pillar's anchor (design s5 F1; 06_functionality_synthesis.md s1.A; Directive 19 :270-273 "Curry's
#   |-FXYZ ... is exactly F(x)->Frame(output:X, effect:Y)"). Curry's functionality operator F - the typed
#   arrow F(X,Y) = "the type of functions X->Y" (Curry 1936 s1) - is NOT re-authored as a parallel tower;
#   the pillar RECOGNIZES the committed SP1 prim:Frame as F. prim:Frame is the unary law's Yoneda point
#   (the typed product Frame(output, effect) the whole realization monad rho is the Kleisli category of;
#   prim:Frame prim:isYonedaPoint true, committed at basicttl/primitives/taiji.ttl:1994), and
#   "Frame is the Yoneda point" = "Frame is Curry's F applied". A fnd:Functionality atom carries the
#   recognition edge fnd:recognizesFrameCarrier onto the committed carrier; the recognition is honest only
#   if that carrier IS the Yoneda-point Frame, never an invented parallel object.
#   DATA CONTRACT (functionality.ttl + SP1): at least one ?f0 a fnd:Functionality exists (non-vacuity
#     anchor, FALSE on the empty foundation graph - fnd:curryFunctionality); at least one fnd:Functionality
#     fnd:recognizesFrameCarrier prim:Frame (the recognition is grounded on the committed carrier); the
#     committed triple prim:Frame prim:isYonedaPoint true holds in the merged graph (SP1); and EVERY
#     fnd:Functionality that fnd:recognizesFrameCarrier ?c recognizes a ?c that is prim:isYonedaPoint true
#     (no functionality recognizes an invented non-Yoneda carrier).
#   PROBE OF RECORD (must flip True->False, mirrored by fnd:FrameRecognitionShape): inject a functionality
#     recognizing an invented carrier - fnd:probeBadFunctionality a fnd:Functionality ;
#     fnd:recognizesFrameCarrier fnd:probeNotAFrame (fnd:probeNotAFrame carries NO prim:isYonedaPoint) -
#     the inner FILTER NOT EXISTS finds it and the ASK is FALSE (a rebuilt parallel F, not the recognized
#     Frame -> RED).
PREFIX fnd:  <urn:silmaril:fnd:#>
PREFIX prim: <urn:silmaril:prim:#>
ASK {
  ?f0 a fnd:Functionality .
  ?fr a fnd:Functionality ; fnd:recognizesFrameCarrier prim:Frame .
  prim:Frame prim:isYonedaPoint true .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?f a fnd:Functionality ; fnd:recognizesFrameCarrier ?c .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?c prim:isYonedaPoint true }
  }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?fN a fnd:Functionality .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?fN fnd:recognizesFrameCarrier ?cN }
  }
}

# EXPECT-TRUE q_functor_variance : the variance bifunctor F(dom,cod) is contravariant in the domain and
#   covariant in the codomain (Curry s4).
#   The s4 subtyping-variance law (design s5 F3/F3'; 06b_curry_lift.md s3.1; Curry 1936 s4: FXY, U subset X,
#   Y subset V => FUV - a function X->Y is also a function U->V). So the arrow type F(X,Y) is a SUBTYPE of
#   F(U,V) exactly when the domain NARROWS (U subset-of X: CONTRAVARIANT) and the codomain WIDENS (Y subset-of
#   V: COVARIANT). Directive 19 :279-281 mandates the function-type algebra carry this variance. The covariant
#   codomain leg is the variance SP1's prim:RealizationTransport already proves as a covariant functor
#   (basicttl/primitives/realization.ttl:2865-2920, q_functor_composition green); the contravariant domain
#   leg is NEW teeth (SP1 has no contravariant structure - the unary law forbids a Frame input coordinate,
#   docs/unary-byte-frame-law.md:686-687 - so F(dom,cod) is a SEPARATE bifunctor object, not prim:Frame the
#   product; design DF-D Opt 2). Variance is checked over a corpus-agnostic witness subtype order fnd:varSubtypeOf
#   (Dog subset-of Animal); an accepted fnd:VarianceStep F(X,Y) <: F(U,V) is well-varied iff U=X or U subset-of X
#   (domain contravariant) AND Y=V or Y subset-of V (codomain covariant).
#   DATA CONTRACT (functionality.ttl): at least one ?s0 a fnd:VarianceStep exists (non-vacuity anchor, FALSE
#     on the empty graph - fnd:varStepValid: F(Animal,Dog) <: F(Dog,Animal), which narrows the domain
#     Animal->Dog and widens the codomain Dog->Animal, both lawful since fnd:typeDog fnd:varSubtypeOf
#     fnd:typeAnimal); NO accepted step widens the domain (every step's target domain ?u satisfies ?u=?x or
#     ?u fnd:varSubtypeOf ?x); and NO accepted step narrows the codomain (every step's source codomain ?y
#     satisfies ?y=?v or ?y fnd:varSubtypeOf ?v).
#   PROBE OF RECORD (must flip True->False, mirrored by fnd:FunctorVarianceShape): inject a domain-WIDENING
#     step - fnd:probeVarStep a fnd:VarianceStep ; fnd:varianceFrom fnd:arrowTypeDogDog ; fnd:varianceTo
#     fnd:arrowTypeAnimalDog (claims F(Dog,Dog) <: F(Animal,Dog), widening the domain Dog->Animal though
#     Animal is NOT a subtype of Dog) - the domain clause fires and the ASK is FALSE (a domain-widening
#     accepted -> RED). Symmetrically, repointing a step to narrow the codomain fires the codomain clause.
PREFIX fnd: <urn:silmaril:fnd:#>
ASK {
  ?s0 a fnd:VarianceStep .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?step a fnd:VarianceStep ; fnd:varianceFrom ?sub ; fnd:varianceTo ?sup .
    ?sub fnd:hasDomainType ?x .
    ?sup fnd:hasDomainType ?u .
    FILTER(?u != ?x)
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?u fnd:varSubtypeOf ?x }
  }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?step2 a fnd:VarianceStep ; fnd:varianceFrom ?sub2 ; fnd:varianceTo ?sup2 .
    ?sub2 fnd:hasCodomainType ?y .
    ?sup2 fnd:hasCodomainType ?v .
    FILTER(?y != ?v)
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?y fnd:varSubtypeOf ?v }
  }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?stF a fnd:VarianceStep .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?stF fnd:varianceFrom ?sf . ?sf fnd:hasDomainType ?sfd . ?sf fnd:hasCodomainType ?sfc }
  }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?stT a fnd:VarianceStep .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?stT fnd:varianceTo ?st2 . ?st2 fnd:hasDomainType ?std . ?st2 fnd:hasCodomainType ?stc }
  }
}

# EXPECT-TRUE q_no_untyped_self_apply : an ungated self-application chi-chi resolves to silm:isProvisional,
#   never a naive proposition (Curry s6 paradox-quarantine).
#   The s6 type-discipline quarantine (design s5; 06b_curry_lift.md s5; Curry 1936 s6: the Russell
#   contradiction E=WQ, chi=[f]N(ff), |-chi-chi=N(chi-chi) arises ONLY from applying functionality F OUTSIDE
#   its proper category - a tacit, "not even plausible" assumption about the functional character of
#   negation). Type/functionality discipline is the quarantine: Directive 19 :293 requires self-application
#   be type-disciplined, never naively self-applicable. A fnd:SelfApplication reifies a self-application
#   f(f)/chi-chi. The teeth enforce TWO INDEPENDENT violation conditions. (a) UNCONDITIONAL: NO
#   self-application - gated or ungated, genuinely resolved or not - may be admitted as a naive proposition
#   (fnd:admittedAsProposition true); admitting chi-chi as a proposition is the exact Curry s6 move, forbidden
#   even for a genuinely-resolved fnd:gatedSelfApplication (only ever PROVISIONALLY named, never a fact).
#   (b) an UNGATED / not-genuinely-resolved self-application (exempt only when GENUINELY RESOLVED, Fix-C) must
#   resolve to silm:isProvisional true (the Praeriehund provisional-naming quarantine: named because it must
#   be named, but not admitted) - or it is a violation; this branch STAYS gated behind the genuine-resolution
#   FILTER NOT EXISTS.
#   FIX-C (genuine resolution, not a mere fnd:passedGuard edge): the earlier tooth exempted a self-application
#   on the mere EXISTENCE of a fnd:passedGuard edge to ANY node, so fnd:passedGuard fnd:propA (an arbitrary
#   UNCONSTRAINED node) admitted the Russell witness. A self-application is now GENUINELY RESOLVED only when
#   its fnd:passedGuard target ?g is a proper gate/quarantine resolution - ?g a fnd:ContractGate OR ?g a
#   fnd:QuarantineResolution - that itself fnd:marksProvisional the self-application, AND the self-application
#   carries silm:isProvisional true; only such a real resolution exempts.
#   DATA CONTRACT (functionality.ttl): at least one ?sa0 a fnd:SelfApplication exists (non-vacuity anchor,
#     FALSE on the empty graph - fnd:chiSelfApplication, the ungated Russell chi-chi, carrying
#     silm:isProvisional true and NO fnd:admittedAsProposition, exempt via the provisional path; plus
#     fnd:gatedSelfApplication which fnd:passedGuard fnd:typedSelfAppGate - a genuine fnd:ContractGate that
#     fnd:marksProvisional it - and itself carries silm:isProvisional true, so it is GENUINELY resolved); and
#     NO self-application carries fnd:admittedAsProposition true (the UNCONDITIONAL branch (a)), and NO
#     not-genuinely-resolved self-application lacks silm:isProvisional true (branch (b)).
#   PROBE OF RECORD - T1 UNCONDITIONAL branch (a) (must flip True->False, mirrored by
#     fnd:SelfApplicationGuardShape): inject fnd:gatedSelfApplication fnd:admittedAsProposition true - a
#     GENUINELY-RESOLVED self-application (it fnd:passedGuard fnd:typedSelfAppGate, a fnd:ContractGate that
#     fnd:marksProvisional it, and carries silm:isProvisional true) admitted as a proposition - now makes the
#     ASK FALSE though it passed GREEN before the split (branch (a) is NOT under the genuine-resolution FILTER
#     NOT EXISTS, so genuine resolution no longer exempts admission-as-a-proposition); this is the Curry s6
#     asymmetry the split closes. Dropping the flag returns the ASK to TRUE.
#   PROBE OF RECORD - branch (b) (the prior Fix-C probe, still biting): inject
#     fnd:chiSelfApplication fnd:passedGuard fnd:propA (an ARBITRARY node, not a fnd:ContractGate /
#     fnd:QuarantineResolution and with no fnd:marksProvisional edge) + fnd:admittedAsProposition true and
#     remove silm:isProvisional true - it is NOT genuinely resolved (the genuine-resolution FILTER NOT EXISTS
#     is satisfied) AND (branch (a)) admitted as a proposition AND (branch (b)) lacks the provisional flag, so
#     the outer FILTER NOT EXISTS finds it and the ASK is FALSE (an ungated chi-chi behind an arbitrary
#     passedGuard, admitted as a proposition -> RED); the pre-Fix-C tooth wrongly exempted this. Equivalently,
#     removing silm:isProvisional true from a non-genuinely-resolved self-application fires branch (b). The
#     branch (b) group re-binds ?sa
#     (?sa a fnd:SelfApplication) BEFORE its FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?sa silm:isProvisional true }, so the guard
#     tests THIS self-application's own provisional flag, per-subject - NOT a lone FILTER over the empty
#     mapping (which, with ?sa unbound, would only ask whether ANY node carries silm:isProvisional).
PREFIX rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#>
PREFIX fnd:  <urn:silmaril:fnd:#>
PREFIX silm: <urn:silmaril:entity#>
ASK {
  ?sa0 a fnd:SelfApplication .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?sa a fnd:SelfApplication .
    {
      # (a) UNCONDITIONAL: admitting a self-application as a NAIVE PROPOSITION is the exact Curry s6 move
      #     -> a violation REGARDLESS of resolution (this branch is NO LONGER under the genuine-resolution
      #     FILTER NOT EXISTS): even a genuinely-resolved gatedSelfApplication + admittedAsProposition true
      #     is RED.
      { ?sa fnd:admittedAsProposition true }
      UNION
      # (b) an UNGATED / not-genuinely-resolved self-application lacking silm:isProvisional true (STILL
      #     gated behind the genuine-resolution FILTER NOT EXISTS, exactly as before).
      {
        FILTER NOT EXISTS {
          ?sa fnd:passedGuard ?g .
          ?g fnd:marksProvisional ?sa .
          ?sa silm:isProvisional true .
          { ?g rdf:type fnd:ContractGate } UNION { ?g rdf:type fnd:QuarantineResolution }
        }
        ?sa a fnd:SelfApplication . FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?sa silm:isProvisional true }
      }
    }
  }
}

# =====================================================================================
# T8 — combinators.ttl EXPECT-TRUE ASKs (design s5, Pillar 4; H. B. Curry, First Properties of
# Functionality in Combinatory Logic, Tohoku Math. J. 41 (1936) 371-401, CITED not committed;
# ledger/W2/algebra_foundation/06b_curry_lift.md s2 + 06_functionality_synthesis.md s1.B). The
# combinatory substrate of the arrow pillar: the agnostic fnd:Combinator progenitor with children
# B/C/W/K/I (each carrying its Curry reduction), the fnd:F_n arity ladder (Def 2.1: F_0=I, F_1=F,
# F_{n+1}=(C.BB_{n+1})F_1 F_n), and the fnd:Compositor Gamma. SYN, cited-from-Curry (the corpus is a
# named-variable lambda corpus, NOT a combinatory-logic corpus - B/C/W/K/I grep-verified ABSENT,
# 06a_functionality_corpus.md s2.3 - so these have no Helios carrier and are honest cited-math atoms).
# Each ASK is non-vacuous (FALSE on the pre-T8 graph) and mirrored by a SHACL tooth proven to bite
# under a probe of record.
# =====================================================================================

# EXPECT-TRUE q_combinator_reduces : each combinator's defining reduction holds (Kxy=x, Ix=x, Wxy=xyy,
#   Cxyz=xzy, Bxyz=x(yz)).
#   The five Curry combinators and their defining reductions (design s5; 06b_curry_lift.md s2.1; Curry
#   1936 combinators B (compose), C (swap), W (duplicate), K (constant), I (identity), axioms (FB)(FC)
#   (FW)(FK)). Each reduction is reified as a fnd:CombinatorReduction over the shared atomic witness
#   terms fnd:argX/argY/argZ (fnd:AtomicTerm), with the applied right-hand sides built as reified
#   fnd:ApplicationTerm nodes (fnd:appFn function part, fnd:appArg argument part, left-associated exactly
#   as combinatory application associates): I x = x; K x y = x; W x y = ((x y) y); C x y z = ((x z) y);
#   B x y z = (x (y z)). The tooth reads the reified term structure by EDGE existence, never a range-
#   inferred rdf:type, so inference=rdfs cannot forge an appFn/appArg edge between two term nodes and
#   defang it (the SP1 defang discipline).
#   DATA CONTRACT (combinators.ttl): at least one ?r0 a fnd:CombinatorReduction exists (non-vacuity
#     anchor, FALSE on the empty foundation graph - fnd:redI/redK/redW/redC/redB); AND no reduction
#     violates its combinator's canonical form - I's and K's fnd:reducesTo IS its fnd:redArg1; W's
#     fnd:reducesTo is the application ((x y) y); C's is ((x z) y); B's is (x (y z)).
#   PROBE OF RECORD (must flip True->False, mirrored by fnd:CombinatorReducesShape): change fnd:redK
#     fnd:reducesTo from fnd:argX to fnd:argY (so K x y = y, the wrong projection) - the K branch's
#     FILTER(?res != ?x) fires and the ASK is FALSE (a wrong reduction -> RED). Equivalently, repointing
#     any applied RHS breaks its structural branch.
PREFIX fnd: <urn:silmaril:fnd:#>
ASK {
  ?r0 a fnd:CombinatorReduction .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?r fnd:reducesCombinator fnd:I ; fnd:redArg1 ?x ; fnd:reducesTo ?res . FILTER(?res != ?x) }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?r fnd:reducesCombinator fnd:K ; fnd:redArg1 ?x ; fnd:reducesTo ?res . FILTER(?res != ?x) }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?r fnd:reducesCombinator fnd:W ; fnd:redArg1 ?x ; fnd:redArg2 ?y ; fnd:reducesTo ?res .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?res fnd:appFn ?in ; fnd:appArg ?y . ?in fnd:appFn ?x ; fnd:appArg ?y . }
  }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?r fnd:reducesCombinator fnd:C ; fnd:redArg1 ?x ; fnd:redArg2 ?y ; fnd:redArg3 ?z ; fnd:reducesTo ?res .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?res fnd:appFn ?in ; fnd:appArg ?y . ?in fnd:appFn ?x ; fnd:appArg ?z . }
  }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?r fnd:reducesCombinator fnd:B ; fnd:redArg1 ?x ; fnd:redArg2 ?y ; fnd:redArg3 ?z ; fnd:reducesTo ?res .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?res fnd:appFn ?x ; fnd:appArg ?in . ?in fnd:appFn ?y ; fnd:appArg ?z . }
  }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?rE fnd:reducesCombinator ?combE .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?rE fnd:reducesTo ?anyE }
  }
}

# EXPECT-TRUE q_fn_ladder : the F_n arity recurrence holds (F_0=I, F_1=F, F_{n+1} folds F_1 and F_n
#   through the compositor); a broken rung -> RED.
#   Curry Def 2.1 (design s5; 06b_curry_lift.md s2.2; Curry 1936: F_0 = I, F_1 = F, F_{n+1} =
#   (C.BB_{n+1}) F_1 F_n) - the n-ary functionality ladder, minted one rung at a time (the corpus's own
#   "add one clause at a time" discipline, 26/03/04:24-50). Each rung is a fnd:NaryFunctionality carrying
#   an xsd:integer fnd:fnIndex; the base rungs carry fnd:fnDefinedAs (F_0 = fnd:I the identity combinator,
#   F_1 = fnd:curryFunctionality the base functionality F of Pillar 4); each successor rung (index >= 2)
#   carries fnd:fnPredecessor (F_n, whose index is one below), fnd:fnBaseCase fnd:fnRung1 (the recurrence
#   always folds in F_1) and fnd:composedVia a fnd:Compositor (the Gamma that composes them). The tooth
#   reads index arithmetic and the recurrence edges, never a range-inferred type, so inference=rdfs
#   cannot defang it.
#   DATA CONTRACT (combinators.ttl): at least one ?fn0 a fnd:NaryFunctionality exists (non-vacuity anchor,
#     FALSE on the empty graph - fnd:fnRung0..fnRung3); the index-0 rung fnd:fnDefinedAs fnd:I and the
#     index-1 rung fnd:fnDefinedAs fnd:curryFunctionality (the two base cases); AND every successor rung
#     satisfies the recurrence - its fnd:fnPredecessor's fnd:fnIndex is exactly one below its own, its
#     fnd:fnBaseCase is fnd:fnRung1, and it is fnd:composedVia a fnd:Compositor.
#   PROBE OF RECORD (must flip True->False, mirrored by fnd:FnLadderShape): change fnd:fnRung2
#     fnd:fnPredecessor from fnd:fnRung1 to fnd:fnRung0 (predecessor index 0, but own index 2, so
#     0+1 != 2, a broken rung) - the predecessor-index branch fires and the ASK is FALSE (a broken
#     recurrence rung -> RED).
PREFIX fnd: <urn:silmaril:fnd:#>
ASK {
  ?fn0 a fnd:NaryFunctionality .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?a fnd:fnIndex 0 . FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?a fnd:fnDefinedAs fnd:I } }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?b fnd:fnIndex 1 . FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?b fnd:fnDefinedAs fnd:curryFunctionality } }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?s fnd:fnPredecessor ?p ; fnd:fnIndex ?i . ?p fnd:fnIndex ?pi . FILTER((?pi + 1) != ?i) }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?s fnd:fnPredecessor ?p ; fnd:fnIndex ?i . FILTER(?i >= 2) FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?s fnd:fnBaseCase fnd:fnRung1 } }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?s fnd:fnPredecessor ?p ; fnd:fnIndex ?i . FILTER(?i >= 2) FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?s fnd:composedVia ?g . ?g a fnd:Compositor } }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?sN fnd:fnIndex ?iN . FILTER(?iN >= 2) FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?sN fnd:fnPredecessor ?pN } }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?sP fnd:fnPredecessor ?pP ; fnd:fnIndex ?iP . FILTER(?iP >= 2) FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?pP fnd:fnIndex ?piP } }
}

# =====================================================================================
# T9 — logic.ttl EXPECT-TRUE ASKs (design s5, Pillar 4 logic sub-floor; H. B. Curry, First Properties
# of Functionality in Combinatory Logic, Tohoku Math. J. 41 (1936) 371-401, CITED not committed;
# ledger/W2/algebra_foundation/06b_curry_lift.md s4 + 06_functionality_synthesis.md). The logic
# stratum of the arrow pillar: propositions P_r / negation N / implication (⊃) + proof terms; the
# K/C/W implication laws (the exact implication face of the T8 combinators K=weakening, C=exchange,
# W=contraction); and the functionality<->implication taiji (Curry Thm 5.8: the exponential/arrow sense
# F(A,B) and the implication sense A⊃B are ONE lexeme with two glossary senses, Directive 16). SYN,
# cited-from-Curry (the corpus is a named-variable lambda corpus with no propositional-implication
# calculus - 06a_functionality_corpus.md - so these are honest cited-math atoms with no Helios carrier,
# never masquerading as a lift). Each ASK is non-vacuous (FALSE on the pre-T9 graph) and mirrored by a
# SHACL tooth proven to bite under a probe of record.
# =====================================================================================

# EXPECT-TRUE q_implication_kcw : the K/C/W implication laws hold (weakening / exchange / contraction).
#   Curry s5's implication laws K/C/W (design s5; 06b_curry_lift.md s4.3; Curry 1936 s5: F is DEFINABLE
#   from ⊃ given the K/C/W implication laws, Thm 5.8). Each law is the implication-face of one T8
#   combinator (K = weakening, C = exchange, W = contraction - the structural rules of the implicational
#   logic, combinators.ttl s2 seam), reified as a fnd:ImplicationLaw carrying fnd:lawCombinator (the T8
#   fnd:K/fnd:C/fnd:W - the seam made a graph fact) and fnd:lawFormula (a reified fnd:Implication tree
#   over the witness propositions fnd:propA/propB/propC via fnd:antecedent / fnd:consequent). The three
#   canonical formulae: K = A ⊃ (B ⊃ A) (weakening: the outer antecedent A reappears as the inner
#   consequent); W = (A ⊃ (A ⊃ B)) ⊃ (A ⊃ B) (contraction: the doubled A in the antecedent contracts to
#   one A in the consequent); C = (A ⊃ (B ⊃ C)) ⊃ (B ⊃ (A ⊃ C)) (exchange: A and B swap around the
#   nesting). The tooth walks the reified implication trees by fnd:antecedent / fnd:consequent EDGE
#   existence, binding the shared propositions by variable identity, never a range-inferred rdf:type, so
#   inference=rdfs cannot forge an implication edge and defang it (the SP1 defang discipline).
#   DATA CONTRACT (logic.ttl): at least one ?l0 a fnd:ImplicationLaw exists (non-vacuity anchor, FALSE on
#     the pre-T9 graph - fnd:lawK / fnd:lawW / fnd:lawC); AND no law departs from its canonical formula -
#     the K-law's fnd:lawFormula is A ⊃ (B ⊃ A) (inner consequent = outer antecedent), the W-law's is
#     (A ⊃ (A ⊃ B)) ⊃ (A ⊃ B) (the shared A and B), the C-law's is (A ⊃ (B ⊃ C)) ⊃ (B ⊃ (A ⊃ C)) (the
#     A/B swap).
#   PROBE OF RECORD (must flip True->False, mirrored by fnd:ImplicationKCWShape): inject a K-law with a
#     non-weakening formula - fnd:probeLawK a fnd:ImplicationLaw ; fnd:lawCombinator fnd:K ;
#     fnd:lawFormula fnd:implAB (the bare A ⊃ B, whose consequent propB is atomic, NOT an implication
#     whose consequent is A) - the K branch's inner FILTER NOT EXISTS finds no A ⊃ (B ⊃ A) structure and
#     the ASK is FALSE (a K-law that is not weakening -> RED).
PREFIX fnd: <urn:silmaril:fnd:#>
ASK {
  ?l0 a fnd:ImplicationLaw .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?lk fnd:lawCombinator fnd:K ; fnd:lawFormula ?f .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS {
      ?f fnd:antecedent ?a ; fnd:consequent ?c .
      ?c fnd:antecedent ?b ; fnd:consequent ?a .
    }
  }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?lw fnd:lawCombinator fnd:W ; fnd:lawFormula ?f .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS {
      ?f fnd:antecedent ?ant ; fnd:consequent ?con .
      ?ant fnd:antecedent ?a ; fnd:consequent ?inner .
      ?inner fnd:antecedent ?a ; fnd:consequent ?b .
      ?con fnd:antecedent ?a ; fnd:consequent ?b .
    }
  }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?lc fnd:lawCombinator fnd:C ; fnd:lawFormula ?f .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS {
      ?f fnd:antecedent ?ant ; fnd:consequent ?con .
      ?ant fnd:antecedent ?a ; fnd:consequent ?bc .
      ?bc fnd:antecedent ?b ; fnd:consequent ?c .
      ?con fnd:antecedent ?b ; fnd:consequent ?ac .
      ?ac fnd:antecedent ?a ; fnd:consequent ?c .
    }
  }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?lF a fnd:ImplicationLaw . FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?lF fnd:lawFormula ?anyF } }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?lC a fnd:ImplicationLaw . FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?lC fnd:lawCombinator ?anyC } }
}

# EXPECT-TRUE q_curry_howard : the exponential/arrow sense and the implication sense coincide on a
#   witness (the Curry-Howard taiji; divergence -> RED).
#   Curry s5's functionality<->implication definability (design s5; 06b_curry_lift.md s4; Curry 1936 s5:
#   F' ≡ [x,y,z](u)(xu ⊃ y(zu)), Thm 5.8 - a function type is a universally-quantified implication; the
#   Curry-Howard ancestor). Directive 16 polysemy: ONE lexeme with two glossary-scoped senses
#   simultaneously - the ARROW sense (the exponential B^A = the fnd:ArrowType F(A,B) of functionality.ttl,
#   T7) and the IMPLICATION sense (A ⊃ B = a fnd:Implication) - the SAME object. A fnd:CurryHowardCorrespondence
#   reifies the taiji, carrying fnd:arrowSense (an fnd:ArrowType) and fnd:implicationSense (an
#   fnd:Implication); the two senses COINCIDE iff the arrow type's fnd:hasDomainType is the fnd:WitnessType
#   the implication's fnd:antecedent denotes (via the propositions-as-types bridge fnd:propType) AND the
#   arrow type's fnd:hasCodomainType is the type the implication's fnd:consequent denotes. The tooth reads
#   the reified correspondence and the propType bridge by EDGE existence, never a range-inferred type, so
#   inference=rdfs cannot defang it (the SP1 defang discipline).
#   DATA CONTRACT (logic.ttl + functionality.ttl): at least one ?ch0 a fnd:CurryHowardCorrespondence exists
#     (non-vacuity anchor, FALSE on the pre-T9 graph - fnd:chWitness: arrow sense F(Animal,Dog) reusing the
#     committed fnd:arrowTypeAnimalDog, implication sense Animal ⊃ Dog = fnd:implAnimalDog); NO correspondence
#     diverges on the domain (every arrow domain type is propType-denoted by the implication antecedent); and
#     NO correspondence diverges on the codomain (every arrow codomain type is propType-denoted by the
#     implication consequent). fnd:propAnimal fnd:propType fnd:typeAnimal and fnd:propDog fnd:propType
#     fnd:typeDog carry the bridge.
#   PROBE OF RECORD (must flip True->False, mirrored by fnd:CurryHowardShape): inject a divergent
#     correspondence - fnd:probeCh a fnd:CurryHowardCorrespondence ; fnd:arrowSense fnd:arrowTypeAnimalDog ;
#     fnd:implicationSense fnd:implDogAnimal (the arrow F(Animal,Dog) paired with the implication Dog ⊃ Animal:
#     the arrow domain typeAnimal but the antecedent propDog denotes typeDog, a domain divergence) - the domain
#     clause fires and the ASK is FALSE (the two senses do not coincide -> RED).
PREFIX fnd: <urn:silmaril:fnd:#>
ASK {
  ?ch0 a fnd:CurryHowardCorrespondence .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?ch fnd:arrowSense ?arr ; fnd:implicationSense ?impl .
    ?arr fnd:hasDomainType ?dt .
    ?impl fnd:antecedent ?ant .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?ant fnd:propType ?dt }
  }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?ch fnd:arrowSense ?arr ; fnd:implicationSense ?impl .
    ?arr fnd:hasCodomainType ?ct .
    ?impl fnd:consequent ?con .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?con fnd:propType ?ct }
  }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?chA a fnd:CurryHowardCorrespondence .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?chA fnd:arrowSense ?arrA . ?arrA fnd:hasDomainType ?adA . ?arrA fnd:hasCodomainType ?acA }
  }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?chI a fnd:CurryHowardCorrespondence .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?chI fnd:implicationSense ?implI . ?implI fnd:antecedent ?iaI . ?implI fnd:consequent ?icI }
  }
}

# EXPECT-TRUE q_proof_term_typed : every proof term is typed by the implication it proves (a proof term
#   whose type isn't the implication it claims -> RED).
#   The terms-as-proofs face of Curry-Howard (design s5; 06b_curry_lift.md s4; Curry 1936 s5). Under the
#   taiji a proof of an implication A ⊃ B is a function of type F(A,B): a fnd:ProofTerm carries
#   fnd:provesImplication (the fnd:Implication it witnesses) and fnd:proofTermType (its fnd:ArrowType). The
#   proof term is well typed iff its arrow type's fnd:hasDomainType is the fnd:WitnessType the proved
#   implication's fnd:antecedent denotes (via fnd:propType) AND its arrow type's fnd:hasCodomainType is the
#   type the proved implication's fnd:consequent denotes - the inhabitant-level coincidence complementing
#   q_curry_howard's constructor-level one. The tooth reads the proof term, the implication tree and the
#   propType bridge by EDGE existence, never a range-inferred type (the SP1 defang discipline).
#   DATA CONTRACT (logic.ttl): at least one ?pt0 a fnd:ProofTerm exists (non-vacuity anchor, FALSE on the
#     pre-T9 graph - fnd:proofAnimalDog: fnd:provesImplication fnd:implAnimalDog (Animal ⊃ Dog),
#     fnd:proofTermType fnd:arrowTypeAnimalDog (F(Animal,Dog))); NO proof term diverges on the domain (its
#     arrow domain type is propType-denoted by the proved antecedent); and NO proof term diverges on the
#     codomain (its arrow codomain type is propType-denoted by the proved consequent).
#   PROBE OF RECORD (must flip True->False, mirrored by fnd:ProofTermTypedShape): inject a mistyped proof
#     term - fnd:probeProof a fnd:ProofTerm ; fnd:provesImplication fnd:implAnimalDog ; fnd:proofTermType
#     fnd:arrowTypeDogAnimal (claims to prove Animal ⊃ Dog but is typed F(Dog,Animal): the arrow domain
#     typeDog, but the proved antecedent propAnimal denotes typeAnimal) - the domain clause fires and the
#     ASK is FALSE (a proof term whose type isn't the implication it claims -> RED).
PREFIX fnd: <urn:silmaril:fnd:#>
ASK {
  ?pt0 a fnd:ProofTerm .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?pt fnd:provesImplication ?impl ; fnd:proofTermType ?arr .
    ?arr fnd:hasDomainType ?dt .
    ?impl fnd:antecedent ?ant .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?ant fnd:propType ?dt }
  }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?pt fnd:provesImplication ?impl ; fnd:proofTermType ?arr .
    ?arr fnd:hasCodomainType ?ct .
    ?impl fnd:consequent ?con .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?con fnd:propType ?ct }
  }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?ptA a fnd:ProofTerm .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?ptA fnd:proofTermType ?arrA . ?arrA fnd:hasDomainType ?adA . ?arrA fnd:hasCodomainType ?acA }
  }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?ptI a fnd:ProofTerm .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?ptI fnd:provesImplication ?implI . ?implI fnd:antecedent ?iaI . ?implI fnd:consequent ?icI }
  }
}


# =====================================================================================
# T10 — reanchor.ttl EXPECT-TRUE ASKs (design s7 the additive re-anchor; ledger/W2/algebra_foundation/
# 05_reanchor_surface.md). SP1/SP2/SP3 re-anchor ONTO the foundation ADDITIVELY - new grounding EDGES
# (fnd:groundsInSet / fnd:groundsInAlgebra / fnd:groundsInSpace / fnd:functionalityOf), rebuild nothing;
# the ONE genuine is-a build is aob:SealedGroup rdfs:subClassOf fnd:Group, teeth-proved a real group.
# =====================================================================================


# EXPECT-TRUE q_reanchor_additive : every prior-floor grounding is an EDGE onto a genuine structure; no rebuild.
#   The additive re-anchor (design s7; 05_reanchor_surface.md s4: 15/16 rows additive). SP1/SP2/SP3 are ALREADY
#   algebra-shaped (Directive 18 last bullet); re-anchoring means adding fnd:groundsIn* / fnd:functionalityOf
#   EDGES from the committed carriers up into the foundation, plus the ONE genuine subclass edge
#   aob:SealedGroup rdfs:subClassOf fnd:Group - no committed structure is rebuilt and (proven by the runner
#   keeping SP1/SP2/SP3 green + git untouched) no prior triple is removed. This tooth makes the additive
#   discipline a GRAPH FACT: the representative re-anchor edges of ALL FOUR grounding predicates exist -
#   the three set/algebra/functionality siblings AND the fourth space sibling at full PARITY (SP1 prim:Octet
#   into a fnd:Set, prim:ByteVector into a fnd:AlgebraicStructure, prim:Frame typed by Curry's F; SP3
#   crs:GeographicPlaneGeometer into a fnd:MetricSpace via fnd:groundsInSpace; SP2 aob:SealedGroup is-a
#   fnd:Group, aob:HashDigest into a fnd:Set; SP3 crs:CarrierProduct into a fnd:Set, crs:CoordinateDerivation
#   typed by F), AND every fnd:groundsInAlgebra edge lands on a GENUINE (Sigma,E) presented-algebra rung (one
#   carrying a fnd:hasSignature) AND every fnd:groundsInSpace edge lands on a GENUINE space object (one
#   carrying a space-structure edge - fnd:hasPoint / fnd:hasDistanceAssertion of a fnd:MetricSpace,
#   fnd:hasTessellationVertices of a fnd:PerceptualTessellation, or fnd:hasCarrierSet / fnd:hasOpenSet of a
#   fnd:TopologicalSpace) - never on a bare non-matching node that would be a rebuild-in-disguise. The space
#   clause reads EDGE existence of a genuine space-structure edge, NOT the range-inferred rdf:type
#   fnd:MetricSpace (which inference=rdfs WOULD materialise onto any fnd:groundsInSpace target and defang a
#   type check) - the same defang discipline the fnd:hasSignature algebra clause uses. Edge-existence throughout.
#   DATA CONTRACT (reanchor.ttl): the EIGHT representative additive edges above exist (FALSE on the pre-T10
#     graph, where none do - the non-vacuity anchor); NO fnd:groundsInAlgebra edge targets a structure
#     lacking a fnd:hasSignature (every algebra grounding lands on a real rung); and NO fnd:groundsInSpace
#     edge targets a structure lacking a space-structure edge (every space grounding lands on a real space).
#   PROBE OF RECORD (each must flip True->False, mirrored by fnd:ReanchorAdditiveShape):
#     (algebra) fnd:probeBadAlgebraGrounding fnd:groundsInAlgebra fnd:setBit2 (a fnd:Set, no fnd:hasSignature)
#       - the algebra FILTER NOT EXISTS finds it and the ASK is FALSE (a rebuild-in-disguise -> RED);
#     (space-delete) removing the sole crs:GeographicPlaneGeometer fnd:groundsInSpace fnd:metricSpaceWitness
#       edge makes the existence line unsatisfiable -> the ASK is FALSE (the space sibling now has teeth);
#     (space-bad) crs:CoordinateDerivation fnd:groundsInSpace fnd:setBit2 (a fnd:Set, no space-structure
#       edge: a groundsInSpace onto a non-space) - the space FILTER NOT EXISTS finds it -> the ASK is FALSE.
PREFIX fnd:  <urn:silmaril:fnd:#>
PREFIX prim: <urn:silmaril:prim:#>
PREFIX aob:  <urn:silmaril:aob:#>
PREFIX crs:  <urn:silmaril:crs:#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
  prim:Octet fnd:groundsInSet ?so .
  prim:ByteVector fnd:groundsInAlgebra ?sm .
  prim:Frame fnd:functionalityOf ?f1 .
  crs:GeographicPlaneGeometer fnd:groundsInSpace ?sp .
  aob:SealedGroup rdfs:subClassOf fnd:Group .
  aob:HashDigest fnd:groundsInSet ?sh .
  crs:CarrierProduct fnd:groundsInSet ?scp .
  crs:CoordinateDerivation fnd:functionalityOf ?f2 .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?c fnd:groundsInAlgebra ?alg .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?alg fnd:hasSignature ?sig }
  }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?cs fnd:groundsInSpace ?spx .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS {
      { ?spx fnd:hasPoint ?pt } UNION { ?spx fnd:hasDistanceAssertion ?da } UNION
      { ?spx fnd:hasTessellationVertices ?tv } UNION { ?spx fnd:hasCarrierSet ?csx } UNION
      { ?spx fnd:hasOpenSet ?os }
    }
  }
}


# EXPECT-TRUE q_sealedgroup_is_group : the SP2 aob:SealedGroup satisfies the full fnd:Group teeth.
#   The ONE real build of the re-anchor (design s7 / Directive 20 PIN: "the one real build is
#   aob:SealedGroup->fnd:Group teeth-proven, with SP2 SealedGroup a CHILD of a fresh agnostic Group
#   progenitor"; 05_reanchor_surface.md A1/D4). SP2's sealed group NAMES itself a monoid/group OBJECT but
#   materialises only partial axioms (associativity + identity + one aob:retracts inverse; no general binary
#   operation, no closure, no two-sided-inverse-universal, no abelian flag - 05 s2.1). T10 makes it a GENUINE
#   group ADDITIVELY: it declares aob:SealedGroup rdfs:subClassOf fnd:Group and supplies (in reanchor.ttl,
#   never touching the SP2 files) the missing foundation-side group structure over the REAL sealed-group
#   elements - identity aob:witnessAnchor, the four elements typed fnd:AlgebraElement, a CLOSED abelian Z/4
#   Cayley table (fnd:opStructure aob:witnessGroup) honouring the one materialised inverse (inv(description)
#   = replacement, matching aob:retracts), and a two-sided fnd:InversePairing for every element. The reused
#   T4 teeth then bite on the actual sealed group: fnd:MonoidIdentityShape (identity) and fnd:GroupInverseShape
#   (every pairing two-sidedly undoes) fire on aob:witnessGroup / its pairings; this ASK confirms the four
#   Directive-20 group properties together: binary-op present, closure (no product escapes the carrier),
#   two-sided-inverse-universal (every element has a genuine inverse), and the abelian flag (commutativity).
#   DATA CONTRACT (reanchor.ttl): aob:SealedGroup rdfs:subClassOf fnd:Group (FALSE on the pre-T10 graph -
#     the non-vacuity anchor); aob:witnessGroup carries fnd:hasIdentityElement + fnd:isAbelian true + a binary
#     op table; NO product lands outside fnd:hasElement (closure); EVERY fnd:hasElement carries a two-sided
#     inverse pairing to the identity; NO pair violates commutativity.
#   PROBE OF RECORD (must flip True->False, mirrored by fnd:SealedGroupIsGroupShape / reusing fnd:GroupInverseShape):
#     change fnd:sgApp_a_c fnd:opResult from aob:witnessAnchor (e) to aob:witnessExample (b), so a.c = b != e:
#     the inverse pairing (description,replacement) no longer two-sidedly undoes AND the product stays in the
#     carrier but breaks the inverse-universal clause -> the ASK is FALSE (the SealedGroup ceases to be a group).
PREFIX fnd:  <urn:silmaril:fnd:#>
PREFIX aob:  <urn:silmaril:aob:#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
  aob:SealedGroup rdfs:subClassOf fnd:Group .
  aob:witnessGroup fnd:hasIdentityElement ?e ; fnd:isAbelian true .
  ?row0 fnd:opStructure aob:witnessGroup .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?row fnd:opStructure aob:witnessGroup ; fnd:opResult ?r .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { aob:witnessGroup fnd:hasElement ?r }
  }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    aob:witnessGroup fnd:hasElement ?x .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS {
      ?p a fnd:InversePairing ; fnd:pairingModel aob:witnessGroup ; fnd:pairingElement ?x ; fnd:pairingInverse ?y .
      ?xy fnd:opStructure aob:witnessGroup ; fnd:opLeft ?x ; fnd:opRight ?y ; fnd:opResult ?e .
      ?yx fnd:opStructure aob:witnessGroup ; fnd:opLeft ?y ; fnd:opRight ?x ; fnd:opResult ?e .
    }
  }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?ab fnd:opStructure aob:witnessGroup ; fnd:opLeft ?u ; fnd:opRight ?v ; fnd:opResult ?uv .
    ?ba fnd:opStructure aob:witnessGroup ; fnd:opLeft ?v ; fnd:opRight ?u ; fnd:opResult ?vu .
    FILTER(?uv != ?vu)
  }
}

# =====================================================================================
# T11 — the honesty-ledger integration tooth (design s0, the Praeriehund honesty ledger; Directive 20
# HONESTY pin). The one NEW EXPECT-TRUE ASK T11 adds; mirrors fnd:AuthorityTagShape.
# =====================================================================================
# EXPECT-TRUE q_honesty_ledger : every fnd class-like/property atom is honestly classified (exactly one
#   DS/PD/SYN tag) and at least one genuinely-tagged fnd class exists (non-vacuity). This is what makes
#   "every foundation atom carries a DS/PD/SYN authority tag, no SYN atom masquerading as a Helios lift"
#   (design s0, LOAD-BEARING) a graph fact rather than prose. The ASK has a POSITIVE non-vacuity clause -
#   there IS an fnd owl:Class carrying a valid authority tag - so it returns FALSE on an empty graph (no
#   such node) and cannot pass vacuously; AND a NOT-EXISTS clause - NO fnd-namespace owl:Class /
#   owl:ObjectProperty / owl:DatatypeProperty anywhere lacks a single valid tag or carries two distinct
#   tags. Over the committed floor all 77 fnd owl:Class + 122 fnd owl:ObjectProperty + 22 fnd
#   owl:DatatypeProperty carry exactly one tag from {fnd:DS, fnd:PD, fnd:SYN}, so the ASK is TRUE.
#   DATA CONTRACT (the whole authored foundation graph): every fnd owl:Class/ObjectProperty/
#     DatatypeProperty carries exactly one fnd:authority in {fnd:DS,fnd:PD,fnd:SYN}; the enumerated tags
#     fnd:DS/fnd:PD/fnd:SYN are declared (engine.ttl) as the three fnd:AuthorityTag individuals.
#   PROBE OF RECORD (must flip True->False, mirrored by fnd:AuthorityTagShape):
#     (a) inject  fnd:probeUntaggedClass a owl:Class .   (an fnd owl:Class with NO fnd:authority) ->
#         the NOT-EXISTS clause finds the unclassified atom -> the ASK is FALSE (branch (a) of the shape
#         bites, conforms=True->False); OR
#     (b) inject  fnd:probeDoubleTag a owl:Class ; fnd:authority fnd:SYN , fnd:DS .  (a masquerading
#         double-tag) -> the NOT-EXISTS clause finds the two distinct tags -> the ASK is FALSE (branch
#         (b) of the shape bites, conforms=True->False).
PREFIX fnd:  <urn:silmaril:fnd:#>
PREFIX owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
ASK {
  ?a a owl:Class .
  FILTER(STRSTARTS(STR(?a), "urn:silmaril:fnd:#"))
  ?a fnd:authority ?ta .
  FILTER(?ta IN (fnd:DS, fnd:PD, fnd:SYN))
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?x a ?meta .
    FILTER(?meta IN (owl:Class, owl:ObjectProperty, owl:DatatypeProperty))
    FILTER(STRSTARTS(STR(?x), "urn:silmaril:fnd:#"))
    FILTER(
      NOT EXISTS { ?x fnd:authority ?t . FILTER(?t IN (fnd:DS, fnd:PD, fnd:SYN)) }
      || EXISTS { ?x fnd:authority ?p , ?q . FILTER(?p != ?q) }
    )
  }
}


# EXPECT-TRUE q_authority_honest : every DS/PD-tagged atom carries an EXACT-LINE helios/srcy citation on
#   EVERY helios reference (the honesty ledger's OWN bar, self-enforcing; design s0, Directive 20 HONESTY
#   pin). A DS (verbatim-Helios) or PD (proof-derived-from-Helios) tag is only honest when the atom's
#   rdfs:comment carries the source LOCUS WITH ITS LINE(S), so a synthesized atom can never masquerade as a
#   Helios lift merely by wearing a DS/PD tag with a bare-file (no-:line) or absent citation. This is
#   STRONGER than q_honesty_ledger (exactly-one-tag) AND stronger than the prior CONTAINS('helios/srcy/')
#   form, which a bare-file citation with no line silently passed - the hole a hostile review named. The
#   ASK has a POSITIVE non-vacuity clause - there IS a DS/PD atom carrying an EXACT-LINE helios/srcy
#   citation (REGEX "helios/srcy/...*.tex:[0-9]") - so it returns FALSE on an empty graph and cannot pass
#   vacuously; a NOT-EXISTS clause - NO DS/PD atom LACKS an exact-line helios/srcy citation (no citation, or
#   a citation stripped to a bare file); and a SECOND NOT-EXISTS clause - NO DS/PD atom carries ANY
#   bare-file helios/srcy .tex NOT followed by :line (REGEX negative lookahead), so EVERY helios citation on
#   a DS/PD atom pins its line(s). Text-only (REGEX over rdfs:comment), never a range-inferred type - the
#   SP1 defang discipline. Over the swept floor every DS/PD atom (minting engine, structural Set, the
#   Monoid/endomorphism seam vocabulary - incl. fnd:soleObject:36-39 - Site/Sheaf/PerceptualTessellation
#   vocabulary - incl. fnd:overCover/fnd:familyOverB:30-52, fnd:LocalSection:1-9, fnd:MatchingFamily:1-5 -
#   the DS/PD/SYN honesty machinery cited to appendix 37:240) carries an exact-line file:line, so TRUE.
#   DATA CONTRACT (the whole authored foundation graph): every subject of fnd:authority whose value is
#     fnd:DS or fnd:PD has at least one rdfs:comment matching "helios/srcy/...*.tex:START(-END)?" AND no
#     rdfs:comment carrying a bare-file helios/srcy .tex with no :line suffix.
#   PROBE OF RECORD (must flip True->False, mirrored by fnd:AuthorityHonestyShape):
#     (a) retag  fnd:AlgebraicStructure fnd:authority fnd:DS  (its comment cites only Directive 17 + the
#         ledger byte_order worked example, no helios/srcy - the exact SYN-masquerading-as-DS dodge) ->
#         the first NOT-EXISTS clause finds the uncited DS atom -> the ASK is FALSE; OR
#     (b) inject  fnd:probeUncitedDS a owl:Class ; fnd:authority fnd:DS ; rdfs:comment "a direct-source
#         claim with no Helios file:line" .  -> a fresh DS atom with no helios/srcy citation -> FALSE; OR
#     (c) STRIP the :line off a real DS atom's sole citation (fnd:soleObject:36-39 -> bare file) -> the
#         first clause (no lined citation) AND the bare-file NOT-EXISTS clause both fire -> the ASK is FALSE.
PREFIX fnd:  <urn:silmaril:fnd:#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
  ?d fnd:authority ?td .
  FILTER(?td IN (fnd:DS, fnd:PD))
  ?d rdfs:comment ?dc .
  FILTER(REGEX(STR(?dc), "helios/srcy/[^ ,;)]*\\.tex:[0-9]"))
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?x fnd:authority ?tx .
    FILTER(?tx IN (fnd:DS, fnd:PD))
    FILTER NOT EXISTS {
      ?x rdfs:comment ?cx .
      FILTER(REGEX(STR(?cx), "helios/srcy/[^ ,;)]*\\.tex:[0-9]"))
    }
  }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?y fnd:authority ?ty .
    FILTER(?ty IN (fnd:DS, fnd:PD))
    ?y rdfs:comment ?cy .
    FILTER(REGEX(STR(?cy), "helios/srcy/[^ ,;)]*\\.tex(?!:[0-9])"))
  }
}


# EXPECT-TRUE q_ring_add_identity : the additive IDENTITY holds on every two-operation structure (0+x=x, x+0=x) (R7-2).
#   The two-operation line (design s3; 02_algebra_tower.md:134-136 - ring FULLY ABSENT as algebra in Helios).
#   SYN, cited standard ring theory. A Semiring/Ring/Field's additive part is a commutative MONOID (Semiring) /
#   abelian GROUP (Ring/Field), so it MUST carry a two-sided additive identity 0 (fnd:hasZeroElement) with
#   0+x=x AND x+0=x for every element; but the ring reifies via fnd:ringStructure over fnd:hasZeroElement -
#   DISTINCT from the spine fnd:opStructure / fnd:hasIdentityElement that q_monoid_identity walks - so no spine
#   identity tooth reached the ring additive identity: a two-operation structure whose declared zero fails 0+a=a,
#   or which omits the zero, passed GREEN (the round-7 finding-2 hole, additive side). This tooth closes it,
#   mirroring q_monoid_identity over the two-operation table, plus a fnd:Semiring EXISTENCE clause.
#   DATA CONTRACT (algebra_rings.ttl): at least one structure declares fnd:hasZeroElement (non-vacuity anchor,
#     FALSE on the empty graph - fnd:ringModel fnd:hasZeroElement fnd:ringZero with 0+0=0, 0+1=1, 0+2=2, 1+0=1,
#     2+0=2; fnd:fieldModel fnd:hasZeroElement fnd:fieldZero); for EVERY structure ?m with fnd:hasZeroElement ?z,
#     NO additive row of ?m with ?z on the left has a result != its right operand and NO row with ?z on the
#     right has a result != its left operand; and EVERY fnd:Semiring (rdf:type/rdfs:subClassOf*) HAS a zero.
#   PROBE OF RECORD (must flip True->False, mirrored by fnd:RingAddIdentityShape): change fnd:appRingAdd_0_1
#     (0+1) fnd:ringResult from fnd:ringOne to fnd:ringZero, so 0+1 = 0 != 1 - the declared zero fails the
#     left-unit law, the inner UNION finds the offending row, and the ASK is FALSE.
PREFIX rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
PREFIX fnd:  <urn:silmaril:fnd:#>
ASK {
  ?anchor fnd:hasZeroElement ?z0 .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?m fnd:hasZeroElement ?z .
    {
      ?rL fnd:ringStructure ?m ; fnd:ringOp fnd:additiveOp ; fnd:ringLeft ?z ; fnd:ringRight ?x ; fnd:ringResult ?rLr .
      FILTER(?rLr != ?x)
    } UNION {
      ?rR fnd:ringStructure ?m ; fnd:ringOp fnd:additiveOp ; fnd:ringLeft ?x ; fnd:ringRight ?z ; fnd:ringResult ?rRr .
      FILTER(?rRr != ?x)
    }
  }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?sr rdf:type/rdfs:subClassOf* fnd:Semiring .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?sr fnd:hasZeroElement ?zX }
  }
}


# EXPECT-TRUE q_ring_mult_identity : the multiplicative IDENTITY holds on every fnd:Semiring (1*x=x, x*1=x) (R7-2 / Fix-B).
#   The two-operation line (design s3; 02_algebra_tower.md:134-136 - ring FULLY ABSENT as algebra in Helios).
#   SYN, cited standard ring theory. A Semiring's multiplicative part is a MONOID (design two-operation line:
#   'each of the two operations a monoid'), so it MUST carry a two-sided multiplicative identity 1 (fnd:hasOneElement)
#   with 1*x=x AND x*1=x for every element; but the ring reifies via fnd:ringStructure over fnd:hasOneElement -
#   DISTINCT from the spine fnd:opStructure / fnd:hasIdentityElement that q_monoid_identity walks - so no spine
#   identity tooth reached the ring/semiring multiplicative identity: a fnd:Semiring whose declared one fails 1*a=a,
#   or which omits the one, passed GREEN (the round-7 finding-2 hole, multiplicative side; and Fix-B: the EXISTENCE
#   clause quantified only over fnd:Ring, so a unit-less bare fnd:Semiring - itself a multiplicative monoid -
#   escaped). This tooth closes it, mirroring q_ring_add_identity over the fnd:multiplicativeOp rows, plus a
#   fnd:Semiring EXISTENCE clause (Fix-B broadens the existence scope from fnd:Ring to fnd:Semiring, and thus
#   Ring/Field, exactly as q_ring_add_identity already quantifies additive existence over fnd:Semiring).
#   DATA CONTRACT (algebra_rings.ttl): at least one structure declares fnd:hasOneElement (non-vacuity anchor,
#     FALSE on the empty graph - fnd:ringModel fnd:hasOneElement fnd:ringOne with 1*0=0, 1*1=1, 1*2=2, 0*1=0,
#     2*1=2; fnd:fieldModel fnd:hasOneElement fnd:fieldOne with 1*1=1); for EVERY structure ?m with
#     fnd:hasOneElement ?o, NO multiplicative row of ?m with ?o on the left has a result != its right operand and
#     NO row with ?o on the right has a result != its left operand; and EVERY fnd:Semiring (rdf:type/rdfs:subClassOf*
#     - fnd:ringModel and fnd:fieldModel are both fnd:Semiring, each with a declared one) HAS a one.
#   PROBE OF RECORD (must flip True->False, mirrored by fnd:RingMultIdentityShape): change fnd:appRingMul_1_0
#     (1*0) fnd:ringResult from fnd:ringZero to fnd:ringOne, so 1*0 = 1 != 0 - the declared one fails the
#     left-unit law, the inner UNION finds the offending row, and the ASK is FALSE; and (Fix-B) a fresh unit-less
#     fnd:Semiring with NO fnd:hasOneElement makes the fnd:Semiring EXISTENCE clause find it, and the ASK is FALSE.
PREFIX rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
PREFIX fnd:  <urn:silmaril:fnd:#>
ASK {
  ?anchor fnd:hasOneElement ?o0 .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?m fnd:hasOneElement ?o .
    {
      ?rL fnd:ringStructure ?m ; fnd:ringOp fnd:multiplicativeOp ; fnd:ringLeft ?o ; fnd:ringRight ?x ; fnd:ringResult ?rLr .
      FILTER(?rLr != ?x)
    } UNION {
      ?rR fnd:ringStructure ?m ; fnd:ringOp fnd:multiplicativeOp ; fnd:ringLeft ?x ; fnd:ringRight ?o ; fnd:ringResult ?rRr .
      FILTER(?rRr != ?x)
    }
  }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?rg rdf:type/rdfs:subClassOf* fnd:Semiring .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?rg fnd:hasOneElement ?oX }
  }
}


# EXPECT-TRUE q_field_mult_comm : multiplicative COMMUTATIVITY holds on every fnd:Field (a*b = b*a) (R7-1).
#   The two-operation line (design s3 'Field multiplicative part COMMUTATIVE'; 02_algebra_tower.md:134-136 -
#   field FULLY ABSENT as algebra in Helios, only record-field). SYN, cited standard field theory. A fnd:Field's
#   defining upgrade over a fnd:Ring is that its nonzero elements form a COMMUTATIVE group under * (a*b=b*a);
#   the additive side already has q_ring_add_comm, but the MULTIPLICATIVE commutativity SPECIFIC to fnd:Field
#   had NO tooth - a fnd:Field with a*b != b*a passed GREEN (the round-7 finding-1 HIGH hole). This tooth closes
#   it CLASS-GENERAL over every fnd:Field (rdf:type/rdfs:subClassOf* fnd:Field, reaching fnd:fieldModel),
#   mirroring q_ring_add_comm over the fnd:multiplicativeOp rows but SCOPED to fnd:Field (noncommutative
#   rings/semirings are legitimate, so the law is added ONLY at the Field rung, exactly as the design pins it).
#   DATA CONTRACT (algebra_rings.ttl): at least one multiplicative row over some ?m a fnd:Field (non-vacuity
#     anchor, FALSE on the empty graph - the GF(3) multiplicative table over fnd:fieldModel, incl. the distinct
#     pair 1*2=2 / 2*1=2); NO pair (a,b) over ANY fnd:Field-typed model has a*b != b*a.
#   PROBE OF RECORD (must flip True->False, mirrored by fnd:FieldMultCommShape): change fnd:appFieldMul_1_2 (1*2)
#     fnd:ringResult from fnd:fieldTwo to fnd:fieldOne, so 1*2 = 1 while 2*1 = 2 (fnd:appFieldMul_2_1) - the pair
#     (1,2) is non-commutative, the inner EXISTS finds it, and the ASK is FALSE.
PREFIX rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
PREFIX fnd:  <urn:silmaril:fnd:#>
ASK {
  ?mAnchor rdf:type/rdfs:subClassOf* fnd:Field .
  ?anchor fnd:ringStructure ?mAnchor ; fnd:ringOp fnd:multiplicativeOp ; fnd:ringLeft ?la ; fnd:ringRight ?ra ; fnd:ringResult ?resa .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?m rdf:type/rdfs:subClassOf* fnd:Field .
    ?rab fnd:ringStructure ?m ; fnd:ringOp fnd:multiplicativeOp ; fnd:ringLeft ?a ; fnd:ringRight ?b ; fnd:ringResult ?ab .
    ?rba fnd:ringStructure ?m ; fnd:ringOp fnd:multiplicativeOp ; fnd:ringLeft ?b ; fnd:ringRight ?a ; fnd:ringResult ?ba .
    FILTER(?ab != ?ba)
  }
}
